\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Taiwan dollar weak, peso at low.  \b0\par\par\uc2 596 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 04:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, March 22 (Reuters) - Political risks undermined\par the Taiwan dollar and the Philippine peso on Monday, after the\par controversy surrounding Taiwan's weekend presidential elections\par and worries ahead of the Philippine elections in May.\par     The Philippine peso        hit a fresh all-time low of\par 56.45 per dollar, while the Taiwan dollar  fell 0.3\par percent from Friday. Central banks in both countries were\par suspected of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to defend their respective \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Elsewhere, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar       , Korean won\par  , Indonesian rupiah  and Thai baht       , were\par also marginally weaker as the Japanese yen  slid further\par from last week's one-month highs.\par     Traders said markets were wary of testing the Japanese\par authorities' tolerance of a stronger yen, despite the belief\par that their aggressive yen-weakening \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ahead of the\par fiscal year end on March 31 had eased.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Markets also waited for news out of Pakistan, where troops\par have rounded up a group of Islamic militants and their tribal\par allies, possibly including a senior al Qaeda figure whose\par capture could boost the dollar.\par     Analysts dismissed the swings in the regionals, led by the\par yen, as temporary noise and said Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would\par appreciate in the longer term.\par     "The best way to trade Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is to stick to the\par fundamental script. Here, the story for the yen and other Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continues to be bullish," Lehman Brothers said in a\par commentary.\par  \par     "Japanese capital markets are increasingly outperforming\par their G3 peers," it said.\par     Asian trade balances were rising and equity inflows also\par remained strong, the note said.\par     "Avoid getting caught in the noise and be prepared to deal\par with the occasional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hiccup. But as long as the\par fundamentals remain positive, stay long Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par     POLITICAL UNCERTAINTY\par     The Taiwan government said on Sunday the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in markets if necessary to maintain exchange rate\par stability.\par     But President Chen Shui-bian's narrow election victory, a\par puzzling assassination attempt and the large number of invalid\par votes have sparked protests and a call for a recount.\par     Even though the authorities have pledged to limit\par volatility in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and stocks, analysts said the\par election outcome was a negative for the Taiwan dollar.\par     A win by the opposition candidate Lien Chan, whose KMT\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Nationalist Party) holds a slim majority in parliament, would  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 have helped Taiwan make progress with tough banking reforms and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 attracted foreign investment, said UBS strategist Bhanu Baweja.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Taiwan dollar had been among the strongest in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asia earlier this year, rising 3.5 percent from December to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 mid-February. It has since been volatile.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0302 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       107.57         106.86       -0.66\par  Sing dlr        1.6949         1.6903       -0.27\par  Taiwan dlr      33.353         33.253       -0.30\par  Korean won     1159.80        1158.20       -0.14\par  Baht             39.47          39.42       -0.13\par  Peso             56.41          56.38       -0.05\par  Rupiah         8560.00        8557.00       -0.04\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       107.57         107.31       -0.24\par  Sing dlr        1.6949         1.6978       +0.17\par  Taiwan dlr      33.353         33.978       +1.87\par  Korean won     1159.80        1192.00       +2.78\par  Baht             39.47          39.59       +0.29\par  Peso             56.41          55.49       -1.63\par  Rupiah         8560.00        8410.00       -1.75 ((Editing by\par Sonali Desai; vidya.ranganathan@reuters.com; Reuters Messaging:\par vidya.ranganathan.reuters.com@reuters.net; +65 6870 3090)).\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040322e03m000h9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
