\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Taiwan dollar hurt, peso at new low.  \b0\par\par\uc2 637 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 10:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, March 19 (Reuters) - The Taiwan dollar\par fell on Friday after President Chen Shui-bian and\par Vice-President Annette Lu were shot while campaigning on the\par eve of the presidential election.\par     Offshore traders bought the dollar not just against the\par Taiwan dollar but also against the Philippine peso ,\par driving the latter to a fresh record low of 56.38 per dollar.\par     For a report on the peso,\par     The Singapore dollar        and Korean won\par   found some support during the day, as they followed\par the yen's moves and waited for its rally to resume.\par     Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was hurt by the possibility a sympathy\par vote may help the President retain the presidency in the face\par of a strong challenge from the opposition Nationalist Party.\par     The Taiwan dollar hit a low of 33.29 per dollar, a 0.2\par percent drop, after the news broke. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stabilised\par after dealers said they saw the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par market to contain the fall.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "If this increases the chances of the DPP coming to power,\par then I think it is negative for the Taiwan dollar,"\par     "The markets had already expected largely that the KMT is\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 going to win, and if the stock market goes lower then you will  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 see a lot of the good work undone for the Taiwan dollar bulls,"  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said Bhanu Baweja, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with UBS.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The KMT holds a slim majority in the legislature and if the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 president belonged to the same party, it would help Taiwan make  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 progress with tough banking reforms and attract foreign  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 investment, Baweja said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     However he added the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weakness would be limited\par even if the Chen retained the presidency.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par     The rest of the Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spent the day in narrow\par ranges, reassessing the yen's trend and speculation that Japan\par would moderate its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The yen was off Thursday's one-month high of 106.35 per\par dollar, straddling 107.\par     Analysts said the Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sluggishness was a sign\par markets had got ahead of themselves in buying the yen, driving\par it up nearly six percent in 10 days, and were now wary.\par     David Simmonds, markets strategist with the Royal Bank of\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Scotland, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , said the scale of Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 may have moderated but markets were being too aggressive in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 buying the yen.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Other Asian central banks were also likely to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 less, although they would remain watchful ahead of elections in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 many countries, Simmonds said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I do feel we are in the early stages of a shift in balance  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 here, away from such huge levels of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and reserves  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 accumulation and towards a slightly faster pace of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 gains," Simmonds said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "But I am quite sure that CBC (Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ), BOK  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Bank of Korea), MAS (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore) are  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 still vigilant around the fringes of these markets and they are  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 not going to disappear either."  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0826 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       106.86         107.13       +0.25\par  Sing dlr        1.6903         1.6922       +0.11\par  Taiwan dlr      33.253         33.228       -0.08\par  Korean won     1158.20        1159.80       +0.14\par  Baht             39.42          39.46       +0.10\par  Peso             56.38          56.27       -0.20\par  Rupiah         8557.00        8540.00       -0.20\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       106.86         107.31       +0.42\par  Sing dlr        1.6903         1.6978       +0.44\par  Taiwan dlr      33.253         33.978       +2.18\par  Korean won     1158.20        1192.00       +2.92\par  Baht             39.42          39.59       +0.42\par  Peso             56.38          55.49       -1.58\par  Rupiah         8557.00        8410.00       -1.72.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040319e03j00184