\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Off highs, rethinking  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 654 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 05:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , March 19 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  retreated\par from early highs on Friday, following the yen's moves as\par markets reassessed speculation that Japan would moderate its\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The dollar was almost a yen        up from Thursday's\par one-month low of 106.35 per dollar. Late on Thursday it was\par hurt by security concerns after a bomb scare affected train\par services between Britain and France.\par     News that a senior al Qaeda member may have been cornered\par in Pakistan boosted the dollar, as did a view that the yen's\par nearly six percent rally in 10 days may have been too rapid.\par     The Singapore dollar        fell back to 1.6920/30, levels\par seen in Thursday's Asian trading and down from the 1.6861 highs\par struck in offshore deals.\par     The Korean won                   gave up four won from an\par offshore one-month peak near 1,155 per dollar.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The Taiwan\par dollar  was also off a one-month high, of 33.16 per\par dollar, and treaded warily ahead of Saturday's presidential\par elections.\par     Analysts said the sluggishness in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was a sign\par markets had got ahead of themselves in buying the yen, and were\par now wary.\par     "I am convinced that a $50 billion a month run rate of\par (Japanese) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is utterly unsustainable and unwise and\par that we have seen the peak," said David Simmonds, markets\par strategist with the Royal Bank of Scotland, Singapore.\par     "The problem is the temptation to look for extremes, that\par either they continue at the same extraordinary rate of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that they have shown over the last few months,\par which is ridiculous, or that they suddenly disappear\par altogether," he said.\par     ASIA TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  LESS\par     The other Asian central banks were also likely to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par less, although they would remain watchful ahead of elections in\par many countries, Simmonds said.\par     "I do feel we are in the early stages of a shift in balance\par here, away from such huge levels of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and reserves\par accumulation and towards a slightly faster pace of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par gains," Simmonds said.\par     "But I am quite sure that CBC (Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ), BOK\par (Bank of Korea), MAS (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore) are\par still vigilant around the fringes of these markets and they are\par not going to disappear either."\par     The Thai baht        rose in a belated catch-up with the\par region's uptrend but the Indonesian rupiah  was weighed\par down by uncertainty ahead of that country's long election\par period, which begins next month.\par     Bhanu Baweja, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with UBS, said while the\par Korean authorities were managing the won less closely than\par before, they would not let it trade freely until investment and\par employment improved.\par  \par     Moreover, there was a threat from the recent drop in\par leading indicators for Asian exports, he said.\par     "If this situation does not change soon, and growth in\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korean export incomes begins to slow even when domestic economy  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 recovery has not yet shifted into top gear, it will induce the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 authorities to once again be more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventionist\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 market," Baweja said.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0332 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       107.23         107.13       -0.09\par  Sing dlr        1.6930         1.6922       -0.05\par  Taiwan dlr      33.218         33.228       +0.03\par  Korean won     1159.40        1159.80       +0.03\par  Baht             39.39          39.46       +0.18\par  Peso             56.32          56.27       -0.09\par  Rupiah         8565.00        8540.00       -0.29\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       107.23         107.31       +0.07\par  Sing dlr        1.6930         1.6978       +0.28\par  Taiwan dlr      33.218         33.978       +2.29\par  Korean won     1159.40        1192.00       +2.81\par  Baht             39.39          39.59       +0.50\par  Peso             56.32          55.49       -1.47\par  Rupiah         8565.00        8410.00       -1.81.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040319e03j000fa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
