\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Up Late As US Dlr Weakens Versus Regionals  \b0\par\par\uc2 670 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 09:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was markedly stronger against its U.S. counterpart late in Asia Thursday, hitting a three-week high in the early afternoon amid broad-based U.S. dollar weakness against regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Singapore government bond prices were slightly weaker in line with softer U.S. Treasurys prices overnight.  \par \par \uc2 At 0800 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6922, down from S$1.6966 late in Asia Wednesday. It traded a S$1.6895-S$1.6993 range intraday.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's plunge to as low as S$1.6895, its lowest level since Feb. 25, was fueled by heavy selling from various banks, including foreign houses, to cut losses on long U.S. dollar-Singapore dollar positions or to bet on a further fall in the U.S. unit against the local unit, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar has been falling against the yen in Asian trade Thursday and is now trading at Y107.07, down from Y108.25 late in New York Wednesday. The U.S. unit fell as low as Y106.75 during Asian trading.  \par \par \uc2 But local banks immediately bought the U.S. dollar around the psychologically important S$1.6900 level, lifting it back into the low-S$1.6900s. One trader said the domestic banks might have acted on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, although another dealer said the banks were likely trading for their own account.  \par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, the MAS is widely known to be averse to excessive volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, and is suspected to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month to curb the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise when the U.S. dollar slid to a four-year low of S$1.6675.  \par \par \uc2 However, with the U.S. unit's close below S$1.7005 late in New York Wednesday, the U.S. dollar-Singapore dollar pair has triggered a bearish double-top pattern that suggests a fall to at least S$1.6823 in coming days, based on technical analysis.  \par \par \uc2 The S$1.7005 level is the March 9 low between the two tops - the March 4 high of S$1.7193 and the March 12 high of S$1.7180.  \par \par \uc2 Another negative factor for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair in the near term is the U.S. dollar's fall below both its 50-day moving average at S$1.6958 and its 30-day moving average at S$1.6952 in Thursday's Asian session. [ 18-03-04 0812GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Singapore government bond prices fell following the results of a five-year bond auction earlier in the session.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore had sold S$1.3 billion in five-year paper at a relatively high cutoff yield of 2.10%.  \par \par \uc2 Late Thursday, the yield on two-year Singapore government bonds rose to 0.95% from 0.92% late Wednesday. At the longer end of the curve, the yield on 10-year bonds was higher at 2.92% from 2.87%, and the 15-year yield was 3.35% versus 3.34% previously.  \par \par \uc2 The five-year benchmark was bid at 2.00%.  \par \par \uc2 Interest rate swaps were also higher in line with local bond yields. The two-year swap offer was at 1.32% from 1.29% late Wednesday, while the five-year offer was 2.25% versus 2.20%. The 10-year swap offer was 3.23%, up from 3.20%.  \par \par \uc2 The spread between two- and 10-year swaps was unchanged at 191 basis points.  \par \par \uc2 The overnight rate rose to 0.4375% from 0.3750%.  \par \par \uc2 Prices quoted in this report are pre-settlement bids obtained from dealers and are subject to change. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg}}}\par \par \uc2 -By Ron Harui and Kevin Lim, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4150; ron.harui@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Dawn Lye [ 18-03-04 0851GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040318e03i000be\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
