\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Nervous about  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 641 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 04:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , March 10 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were just\par a shade weaker on Wednesday morning with trading still driven\par by wariness over Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and expectations of\par longer-term appreciation in the regionals.\par  \par     As with Japan, markets in Korea and Taiwan worried about\par possible dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by their central banks.\par     Weak Asian equity markets following losses on Wall Street,\par provided further impetus to bearishness on the regionals.\par     Mimicking the yen's decline of over a yen from levels close\par to 110 per dollar in overnight trade, the Sing dollar\par bounced off 1.70 offshore and lost more than half a cent.\par     The Taiwan dollar          was flat around 33.32 per U.S.\par dollar and the Thai baht  was slightly weak.\par     An exception was the Korean won                  , which\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 was about a quarter percent stronger than levels around 1,174  \f28 \par \par \uc2 late on Tuesday. It fell from a three-week high near 1,167 on  \par \par \uc2 Tuesday after the Bank of Korea was believed to have  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Korea and  \par \par \uc2 Taiwan seemed to be aimed at slowing the appreciation in their  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , unlike in Japan, where markets believe the dollar  \par \par \uc2 is being defended at 110 yen.  \par \par \uc2 "Overall, I don't think that the markets' view that the  \par \par \uc2 Korean authorities have adjusted their stance is incorrect,"  \par \par \uc2 said John Cairns, head of research at IDEAglobal Ltd.,  \par \par \uc2 Singapore.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "It is just that the Korean authorities are not going to\par allow sudden and large appreciation."\par     Cairns estimated the Bank of Korea had bought about $200\par million on Monday and over $1 billion on Tuesday and Wednesday,\par to slow the won's gains both against the dollar and the yen.\par     Traders were however betting on longer-term gains in some\par regionals and indicated a preference for buying the Sing dollar\par and the north Asians -- the won and Taiwan dollar.\par     Some traders in Singapore were already positioning for\par heavy inflows that Singapore Telecom  would receive\par when it sells its stake in Belgian telephone operator Belgacom\par          which is preparing for an initial public offering.\par     LESS BULLISH ON BAHT, RUPIAH\par     Elsewhere, the Philippine peso        stayed in a narrow\par 56.15-56.25 range, just above its lifetime low of 56.35 which\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is believed to be defending.\par     The Indonesian rupiah        was near 8,550 per dollar,\par sidelined ahead of parliamentary and presidential elections\par starting from next month.\par     Analysts said they would avoid taking any bets, especially\par bullish ones, on the peso and rupiah because of the political\par risk even though they offered high yields.\par     IDEAglobal's Cairns said he would also be wary of buying\par the baht as the bird flu outbreak had hurt exports and\par authorities seemed reluctant to let the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rise.\par     "The bird flu is not a major worry but it has altered the\par balance of payments significantly enough to suggest that the\par downside on dollar/baht has slowed considerably," Cairns said.\par     The baht was quoted at 39.35/40 a dollar.\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par  Change on the day at   0305 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       111.25         111.18       -0.06\par  Sing dlr        1.7080         1.7020       -0.35\par  Taiwan dlr      33.329         33.327       -0.01\par  Korean won     1171.80        1174.90       +0.26\par  Baht             39.38          39.31       -0.18\par  Peso             56.18          56.18       +0.00\par  Rupiah         8552.00        8548.00       -0.05\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       111.25         107.31       -3.54\par  Sing dlr        1.7080         1.6978       -0.60\par  Taiwan dlr      33.329         33.978       +1.95\par  Korean won     1171.80        1192.00       +1.72\par  Baht             39.38          39.59       +0.52\par  Peso             56.18          55.49       -1.23\par  Rupiah         8552.00        8410.00       -1.66.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040310e03a000jv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
