\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Pinned down by doubts over yen.  \b0\par\par\uc2 668 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 09:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, March 8 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets were\par restless on Monday as doubts swirled about the U.S. dollar's\par global trend and over Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the yen.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar        rose almost a cent, from\par Friday's three-month low of 1.7186, and the Korean won\par   moved in a narrow range around 1,172 per dollar.\par  \par     The baht        was almost unchanged from Thursday's close\par around 39.45 as Thai markets opened after a long weekend.\par     The Thai economy grew a better than expected 2.7 percent in\par the fourth quarter of 2003, helping it to its biggest annual\par expansion in eight years, official data showed on Monday.\par     But, with the yen hitting a five-month low of 112.30 per\par dollar on Friday in New York, markets were taking no chances.\par     While the regionals had indeed parted ways with the yen's\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 three-week fall versus the U.S. dollar, analysts said there was  \f28 \par \par \uc2 a lingering risk that Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen  \par \par \uc2 would continue, and eventually pull down regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "Dollar/yen has to come down and so does dollar/Asia," said\par Bhanu Baweja, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with UBS.\par     "The only risk is that of BOJ \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," he said,\par adding that buying the yen at this time could be likened to\par going against "a moving train."\par     The yen has shed over 3.6 percent of its value against the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar in two weeks. In comparison, the won is up about a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 percent, the Taiwan dollar has lost over half a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 percent and the Singapore dollar is about 1.2 percent down in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 two weeks.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders said cross-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trades, involving short  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 positions in the yen against the regionals, were becoming too  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 crowded and the ambiguity about the yen made things worse.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Markets were also confused about the U.S. dollar's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 direction in major markets after Friday's surprisingly weak  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. jobs data and some comments from European policymakers  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 appreciating the dollar's rebound versus European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While the U.S. dollar climbed against the yen in the face  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 of the jobs data, it fell against other major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  like   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the euro , Swiss franc  and sterling       .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BUY THE RUPIAH  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Elsewhere, the Philippine peso moved in a tight  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 56.32-56.35 per dollar band. It was supported at the 56.35  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 record low by suspicion the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was defending the  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as political uncertainty continued to hurt sentiment.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesian rupiah recovered gradually in opening  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 deals, crossing over from the weaker side of 8,600 to the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Baweja said he would place bets on a rally in the rupiah\par against the dollar, by buying rupiah in the offshore forwards.\par     Bank Indonesia had defended the rupiah from falling past\par 8,600, and hence they might not confuse markets by buying\par dollars too at those levels, he said.\par     "Given BI's greater \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves ammunition compared to\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 recent years, and the high probability of a near-term turn in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar/yen, we see value in selling near-dated dollar/rupiah  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 non-deliverable forwards," he said.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day 0802 GMT   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       112.15         111.20       -0.85\par  Sing dlr        1.7113         1.7143       +0.18\par  Taiwan dlr      33.403         33.424       +0.06\par  Korean won     1173.30        1173.70       +0.03\par  Baht             39.45          39.53       +0.20\par  Peso             56.22          56.33       +0.20\par  Rupiah         8583.00        8592.00       +0.10\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       112.15         107.31       -4.32\par  Sing dlr        1.7113         1.6978       -0.79\par  Taiwan dlr      33.403         33.978       +1.72\par  Korean won     1173.30        1192.00       +1.59\par  Baht             39.45          39.59       +0.34\par  Peso             56.22          55.49       -1.30\par  Rupiah         8583.00 