\par\par \b \uc2 Asia likely to act if dlr falls sharply - Singapore.   \b0\par\par\uc2 285 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2004\par 09:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Feb 26 (Reuters) - Asian central banks were likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to prevent a sharp fall in the U.S. dollar that could threaten demand for the region's exports, a Singapore government economist said on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Friedrich Wu, director, economics division of the Ministry of Trade and Industry, told a news conference that a sharp correction in the U.S. dollar could trigger a sell-off of U.S. dollar assets as well as a rise in U.S. interest rates, which would drag the economy down.   \par \par \uc2 "We believe that Asian central banks are likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to prevent this from occurring as their economies remain highly dependent on U.S. demand," he told reporters after the release of Singapore's economic growth figures.   \par \par \uc2 Asked if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the U.S. dollar continued to slide against the Singapore dollar , a \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS) official declined comment.   \par \par \uc2 "We do not comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy and reiterate we maintain the exchange rate against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and there is no change in that regime," Khor Hoe Ee, an assistant Managing Director at the MAS told the news conference.   \par \par \uc2 Asian central banks hold over $2 trillion worth of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, mostly in dollars. Reserves have risen sharply over the last two years or so as central banks have fought the weakening trend in the U.S. dollar in an attempt to keep their exports competitively priced in the key U.S. market.   \par \par \uc2 The practice has been strongly criticised by European and U.S. policymakers as distorting \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and handing Asia an unfair trade advantage.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040226e02q001e6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
