\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Warns Of Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  To Halt USD Fall  \b0\par\par\uc2 502 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2004\par 02:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--Asian central banks are expected to "\b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily" to slow the U.S. dollar's decline as the region's economies begin to grow again, a top Singapore official said Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The falling U.S. dollar is also a threat to Singapore's export-driven economy, which expanded by 1.1% in 2003 and is expected to grow 3.5%-5.5% this year, said Friedrich Wu, the chief economist at Singapore's Ministry of Trade & Industry.  \par \par \uc2 "A sharp fall of the U.S. dollar under the downward pressure of the twin deficit" could pose a risk to Singapore's economic growth. "But Asian central banks are likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to prevent this."  \par \par \uc2 These are the first public comments from officials in Singapore on the U.S. dollar's decline and indications of a concerted Asian effort to stem the fall.  \par \par \uc2 (MORE)  \par \par \uc2 Asian central banks, including the Bank of Japan, have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to curb the U.S. dollar's sharp decline in recent months. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also said to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has declined to comment on it.  \par \par \uc2 Asian governments are worried a weak U.S. dollar would hurt their exports and therefore hurt economic growth.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's real gross domestic product grew 7.0% in annualized terms in the October-December period, a pace of expansion that marked a 13-year high. The growth was driven by overseas shipments, capital investment to produce those goods and improved consumer outlays.  \par \par \uc2 Malaysia and Thailand have also reported strong economic growth, and expect exports to continue to underpin GDP growth in 2004.  \par \par \uc2 (MORE)  \par \par \uc2 Since the Group of Seven statement in September, the U.S. dollar has fallen by 20% against the euro and by 5.4% against the Singapore dollar.  \par \par \uc2 A senior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official also said Thursday that Singapore's inflation rate will likely rise slightly to 0.5%-1.5% this year compared with 0.5% in 2003 as economic growth picks up.  \par \par \uc2 The statement by Khor Hoe Ee, an assistant managing director at the MAS, reiterates the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's outlook for the consumer price index issued late last year.  \par \par \uc2 "As economic activity picks up, it's not unreasonable to expect inflation to rise from last year," he told reporters.  \par \par \uc2 On the exchange rate, which the MAS controls, Khor remained tightlipped about any possible change to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current neutral monetary policy stance.  \par \par \uc2 The MAS continued to keep the Singapore dollar within the trade-weighted policy band it has set for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The extent of this band isn't made known to the public.  \par \par \uc2 "There has been no change to that," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Khor didn't discuss implications for monetary policy from the expanding economy, saying the policy stance will be announced in April.  \par \par \uc2 -By Izham Ahmad, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-415-4150; izham.ahmad@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Ryan Woo  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040226e02q00012\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
