\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Edge up but off recent highs.  \b0\par\par\uc2 735 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Februar 2004\par 04:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Feb 16 (Reuters) - Most Asian regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  edged up on Monday but were still shy of recent\par highs as the U.S. dollar steadied against major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     A one-day holiday in the United States was also seen\par sapping trading interest, lowering volume and restricting\par ranges in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, dealers said.\par     The Singapore dollar        traded as high as 1.6730 per\par U.S. dollar, from late Friday's 1.6745 but was far from its\par four-year peak of 1.6675 hit on Thursday.\par     The Taiwan dollar          tested 33.10 per U.S. dollar,\par its strongest in 18-months which was also hit on Thursday. The\par South Korean won             rose to a new four-month\par high of 1,157.6 in local trade, but was off Friday's offshore\par high of 1,156.0.\par     Dealers in Singapore said the won was helped after the Bank\par of Korea said authorities planned to ease restrictions,\par introduced last month, on domestic institutions' trading of\par non-deliverable forwards.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The move was aimed at curbing\par speculation.\par     The Thai baht        was steady at around 38.90 per dollar,\par against last week's one-month high of 38.80. The Indonesian\par rupiah  hugged a tight range around 8,400 per dollar.\par  \par     The Philippine peso        lingered at around 56.10 per\par dollar, not far from its all-time low of 56.22 hit in January.\par     "After last week's run (to new highs), the market needs\par fresh factors," said a dealer of regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Dealers said fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , to curb\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength, and volatility due to low volume was\par expected to keep players cautious across the region.\par     PRESSURE TO APPRECIATE\par     However Philip Wee, strategist at DBS Bank in Singapore\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said despite the caution markets were more confident that most  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , backed by strong economic performance and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 diplomatic pressure, would appreciate in the medium term.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We believe that Asia will be coming under pressure to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 rebalance the asymmetric weakness in the dollar's adjustment to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 address global imbalances," said Wee, referring to the fact  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 that over the last two years the U.S. unit has depreciated  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 mainly against \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Europe, Australia, New Zealand and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Canada.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gained last week following the Group of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Seven industrial powers' implicit call on Asia to allow  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 appreciation against the dollar.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's comments on  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wednesday added to the dollar's woes. Greenspan said there was  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 no rush to tighten monetary policy and that a weak dollar would  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 help narrow the country's large current account deficit.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Dealers said for players in Asian regionals, a test of 105\par yen  could provide a fresh cue to sell U.S. dollars.\par     European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Jean-Claude Trichet's\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 testimony before the European Parliament, due later on Monday,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 was also seen as an opportunity for Europe, worried over the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 euro's strength, to take a jab at China's policy to keep the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 yuan virtually pegged at 8.28 per dollar.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Speculation over this drove the yuan non-deliverable  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 forwards premium back to its recent high of 1,200  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 points on the three-month tenor . The premium on the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 one-year tenor was around 4,450 points, implying an expected  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 appreciation of close to 5.7 percent in a year's time.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We believe that as the pressure on yen and yuan intensify,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the mileage may be in selling dollars against Asia, except for  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the Philippine peso," Wee said.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day 0256 GMT   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       105.44         105.35       -0.09\par  Sing dlr        1.6735         1.6745       +0.06\par  Taiwan dlr      33.103         33.130       +0.08\par  Korean won     1157.70        1160.10       +0.21\par  Baht             38.87          38.91       +0.10\par  Peso             56.06          56.10       +0.07\par  Rupiah         8395.00        8407.00       +0.14\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest 