\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Off highs after week of gains.   \b0\par\par\uc2 802 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2004\par 09:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Feb 13 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pulled back\par from recent highs on Friday as players reduced short U.S.\par dollar positions after repeated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par during the week and ahead of a long U.S. weekend.\par     Dealers said profit-taking emerged after a week of\par reasonable gains that began with the Group of Seven industrial\par powers' implicit call on Asia to allow appreciation against the\par dollar.\par     Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's comments on\par Wednesday added to the dollar's woes. Greenspan said there was\par no rush to tighten monetary policy and that a weak dollar would\par help narrow the country's large current account deficit.\par     The Singapore dollar        pulled back almost a full cent\par from Thursday's four-year high of 1.6675 per U.S. dollar, the\par South Korean won             was off its four-month high\par of 1,159.9 and the Taiwan dollar  at one point was down\par a quarter percent from Thursday's 18-month high of 33.10.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Thai baht        went as low as 38.94 per dollar, off a\par one-month high of 38.80, the Indonesian rupiah  was on\par the weaker side of the 8,400 per dollar level and the\par Philippine peso  hit 56.105 per dollar, its lowest in\par about a week.\par     TESTING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESOLVE\par     Dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said suspected dollar-buying\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar throughout the week,\par mainly through local banks, turned aggressive on Thursday.\par     They said local banks were spotted early Friday at around\par the 1.6730 level, prompting more covering of short dollar\par positions but interest to buy the Sing dollar was also seen\par below 1.6760.\par     "The Sing dollar was testing the upper boundary of the\par estimated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tolerance band," said Thio Chin Loo,\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at BNP Paribas in Singapore.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore targets the Sing dollar\par within an undisclosed trade-weighted policy band to ensure it\par remains competitive against those of major trade partners.\par     "The rebound from there and the congestive tone in the U.S.\par dollar against other majors suggest that spot dollar/Sing is\par likely to range between 1.6680 to 1.6800 in the near term,"\par Thio said.\par     Dealers said the South Korean won repeatedly ran into what\par they believe were \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -driven dollar purchases at the\par 1,160 per dollar level.\par     The Taiwan dollar was capped at levels just shy of 33.10.\par     Dealers said even after losses on early Friday, most Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were hanging on to a large part of their recent\par gains.\par     The Singapore dollar has gained about 1.4 percent so far\par this year, against near two percent gains for the whole of\par 2003. The Taiwan dollar has gained about 2.5 percent, against\par 2.24 percent in 2003 and the Korean won has risen by 2.8\par percent versus a depreciation of close to one percent last\par year.\par     YUAN MOVE\par     Taking a cue from the regional bias, the Chinese yuan\par non-deliverable forwards  premium traded at around\par 1,100 points on the three-month tenor , versus 1,200\par points on Thursday.\par     The premium on the one-year tenor was around 4,200 points,\par against a high of 4,450 points on Thursday. At 4,200 points the\par premium implies an expected appreciation of slightly above five\par percent in the yuan  in a year's time.\par     A Reuters poll of 25 analysts from banks, investment houses\par and consultancies in Asia, Europe and the United States showed\par China was expected to change its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regime this year\par which would allow the yuan to strengthen at least a little.\par     "More appreciation pressure on the yen and Asian regionals\par will be exerted as a result of the China move towards\par flexibility," said Bhanu Baweja, strategist at UBS.\par     "We have not factored this in our \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  forecasts but\par recognise that this poses an upside risk to Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par  Change on the day 0810 GMT\par  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       105.35         105.36       +0.01\par  Sing dlr        1.6745         1.6724       -0.13\par  Taiwan dlr      33.130         33.129       -0.00\par  Korean won     1160.00        1160.40       +0.03\par  Baht             38.91          38.86       -0.13\par  Peso             56.10          55.98       -0.21\par  Rupiah         8407.00        8410.00       +0.04\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       105.35         107.31       +1.86\par  Sing dlr        1.6745         1.6978       +1.39\par  Taiwan dlr      33.130         33.978       +2.56\par  Korean won     1160.00        1192.60       +2.81\par  Baht             38.91          39.59       +1.73\par  Peso             56.10          55.49       -1.09\par  Rupiah         8407.00        8410.00       +0.04.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040213e02d001e2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
