\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Sing, Taiwan dlr at new highs, cbanks eyed.   \b0\par\par\uc2 637 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Februar 2004\par 04:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Feb 11 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pushed\par higher against the U.S. dollar on Wednesday on growing\par speculation that central banks may have less resistance to\par exchange rate strength.\par     Dealers said that while the presence of central banks was\par being felt across the region, there was a growing feeling that\par the gradual gains this week showed they were smoothing the rise\par rather than defending levels.\par     The Singapore dollar rose past the 1.6700 per dollar level\par to briefly touch a new four-year high of 1.6690. It pulled back\par to 1.6720 at the first sight of strong U.S. dollar bids from\par local banks, which sparked talk the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was in the\par market.\par     "The fear (of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) is there and maybe they (the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) were in the market," said a\par dealer at a foreign bank in Singapore.\par     "But at the same time no one is sure if they have actually\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  If anything, gains this week suggest they have\par eased a bit on dollar bids."\par  \par     The Taiwan dollar hit a fresh 18-month high of 33.121 per\par dollar, despite concerns about possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The South Korean won extended its four-month highs to\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1,610.6 per dollar, even as a finance ministry official said   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 authorities were concerned about "excessive" volatility in   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 exchange rates and planned to take action if necessary.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We are worried that intensifying speculation on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 rates has caused excessive moves in the exchange rates," the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 official told Reuters.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He also said there had been no change in the government's   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 stance that exchange rates should reflect the country's   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 economic fundamentals.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Still, dealers said there was growing talk in the market   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 that the new finance minister, Lee Hun-jai, named late on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tuesday, would be more tolerant to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 G7 FALL-OUT   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 David Simmonds, strategist at Royal Bank of Scotland in   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore, said the Bank of Korea was unlikely to step   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 completely out of the way of the won's rise against the dollar,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 but central banks appeared to be less eager to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "This is kind of a post-G7 fall-out the market was looking   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 for," he said, referring to the weekend meeting of the Group of   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Seven industrial powers that made an implicit call on the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 region to allow more exchange rate flexibility.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Our anticipated change in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy appears to   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 be materialising," wrote James Malcolm, strategist at JP Morgan   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chase, in a morning note.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "Policy signals are tilting increasingly towards smoothing\par the pace of decline, rather than defending specific levels."\par     Simmonds said the same was true for the Singapore dollar,\par unless the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped in to conduct an aggressive\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     On the South Korean won, Simmonds said the crucial factor\par was its cross against the Japanese yen which had been testing\par the 11-per-won level, up from lows around 11.20 won last month.\par     The speculation of a shift in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bias in the region\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 pushed the Chinese yuan non-deliverable forwards premium to   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1,200 points on the three-month tenor versus 850 points last   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 week. The premium on one-year tenor reached 4,450 points. That   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 suggested the market expected the yuan to appreciate by about   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 5.5 percent in a year's time.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Encouraged by its peers, the Thai baht rose to 38.91 per   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar, its strongest in nearly a month. It had touched 38.85   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in offshore trade.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine peso held steady at around 55.85 per dollar,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 although dealers in Manila said the market was cautious after   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 official campaigning for the May presidential election kicked   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 off on Tuesday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesian rupiah held on to three-week highs on the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 stronger side of the 8,400 per dollar level.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040211e02b000xg\par }\p