\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Eye new highs despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  talk.  \b0\par\par\uc2 688 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 2004\par 04:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Feb 10 (Reuters) - Asian regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par rose versus the U.S. dollar on Tuesday even as dealers said\par they suspected central banks were actively trying to curb the\par gains.\par     They said the market was testing Asian central banks'\par resolve after the Group of Seven industrial powers made an\par implicit call on Asian countries at a weekend meeting to let\par their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciate against the dollar.\par     The Singapore dollar        rose to 1.6827 per dollar, up\par from late Monday's 1.6843. In New York trade the Sing dollar\par had touched 1.6820, a level last seen in January 2000.\par     Dealers said mainly foreign banks and funds were bidding\par the Sing dollar higher despite a bout of strong U.S. dollar\par purchases by local banks at around 1.6830 on Monday. That had\par raised suspicion authorities were trying to curb the rise.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The South Korean won                   rose more than a\par quarter percent to touch a four-month high of 1,162.1 per\par dollar, before talk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  capped the\par rise.\par     Dealers said the won's rise was powered by dollar sales by\par foreign investors who had been buying Korean stocks in recent\par sessions. Foreign investors have bought a net 4.2 trillion won\par worth of Korean stocks so far this year.\par     The Taiwan dollar          rose to 33.17 per U.S. dollar,\par its highest since July, even as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continued to\par place bids for U.S. dollars.\par     "There are the stock purchases and then the central banks'\par emphasis is more on smoothing rather than protecting levels,"\par said James Malcolm, strategist at JP Morgan Chase in Singapore.\par  \par     "Its a fairly broad-based U.S. dollar weakness and Asian\par appreciation," he said.\par     Malcolm said the region's improving economic outlook and\par the growing diplomatic pressure as reflected by the G7\par statement would push Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  higher.\par     "Central banks will also be less demanding in terms of\par trying to prevent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strengthening," he said.\par     The G7 call, similar to one made in September, comes\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 against the backdrop of continued resistance by Asian central  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 banks, including Japan's, to significant appreciation in their  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . China has virtually pegged its yuan at  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 about 8.28 to the U.S. dollar.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In contrast most major European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the Australian   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar  and the Canadian dollar        have risen to\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 multi-year highs. The euro has risen some 10 percent  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 against the dollar since September.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Chinese yuan non-deliverable forwards traded  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 at a premium of 850 points on the three-month tenor  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 , versus 1,000 points on Monday. The premium on the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 one-year tenor eased back to around 3,800 points from Monday's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 high of 4,200.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Elsewhere, the Thai baht clung to a familiar range  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 around the 39 per dollar level, after hitting a three-week high  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 of 38.95 in offshore trade.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dealers said mainly foreign banks and exporters were  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 looking to sell dollars against the baht and more dollar sales  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 were likely after a recent surge in foreign purchases of local  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 stocks.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine peso edged lower as official  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 campaigning for the presidential elections in May kicked off.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesian rupiah was steady at around 8,430 per  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day 0335 GMT   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       105.62         105.57       -0.05\par  Sing dlr        1.6821         1.6843       +0.13\par  Taiwan dlr      33.170         33.227       +0.17\par  Korean won     1162.20        1166.20       +0.34\par  Baht             38.99          39.01       +0.05\par  Peso             55.91          55.87       -0.07\par  Rupiah         8430.00        8431.00       +0.01\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       105.62         107.31       +1.60\par  Sing dlr        1.6821         1.6978       +0.93\par  Taiwan dlr      33.170         33.978       +2.44\par  Korean won     1162.20        1192.60       +2.62\par  Baht             38.99          39.59       +1.53\par  Peso             55.91          55.49       -0.75\par  Rupiah         8430.00        8410.00       -0.24.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument 