\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Off lows, but  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  worries persist.  \b0\par\par\uc2 594 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Januar 2004\par 10:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Jan 16 (Reuters) - Most Asian regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  recovered from their recent lows on Friday, except\par for the Singapore dollar, which fell even as economic data\par delivered a bullish surprise.\par     The Singapore dollar        tested 1.70 per U.S. dollar, as\par the market gave a muted response to unexpectly strong exports\par data for December.\par     Exports, excluding oil, rose for a second straight month,\par gaining 3.9 percent from November to beat analysts' forecasts\par and push total 2003 exports up 15.1 percent.\par     Dealers said any positive impact from the data had been\par absorbed by Singapore banks, which had been buying U.S. dollars\par since Friday morning, sparking fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "When local banks in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are buying dollars\par aggressively, others don't usually want to test and see who is\par behind the order," said a dealer at a European bank.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Overall sentiment on Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stayed depressed\par because of recent moves in South Korea and Thailand to curb the\par strength of the won and baht.\par     South Korea imposed limits on Thursday on domestic\par financial institutions' trade with the offshore non-deliverable\par forward market -- a move seen aimed at curbing the won's\par   rise.\par  \par     On the same day the Bank of Thailand declared that it had\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  recently to stem the baht's  gains.\par     Those actions have doused hopes of gains against the U.S.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar ahead of the early February Group of Seven meeting that  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 is expected to discuss weakness of the U.S. dollar, the euro's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 rise to record highs and Asia's policy of keeping its  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weak.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dealers said with U.S. markets closed on Monday and with  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese New Year holidays in the region next week, most players  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 prefered to square out of their short U.S. dollar positions.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The market is growing nervous about complaints on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 appreciation by authorities and looked to book profits on its  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 short dollar positions," said Bhanu Baweja, strategist at UBS  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in Singapore.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The won on Friday eased to 1,188.5 per dollar, before  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 recovering to 1,186.0 at the close of local trade. On Thursday  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 it briefly hit 1,192.5 per dollar, its weakest in nearly two  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 weeks.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The baht traded on the weaker side of 39 per dollar before  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 edging slightly stronger at 38.97. It hit a one-week low of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 39.04 on Thursday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Taiwan dollar finished local trade a touch  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 higher at 33.685 per U.S. dollar from Thursday's close of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 33.70, helped by exporter demand for local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ahead of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the Chinese New Year holidays starting next week.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day 0845 GMT   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       105.95         106.19       +0.23\par  Sing dlr        1.6996         1.6956       -0.24\par  Taiwan dlr      33.692         33.700       +0.02\par  Korean won     1186.00        1186.10       +0.01\par  Baht             38.94          38.99       +0.13\par  Peso             55.46          55.50       +0.07\par  Rupiah         8344.00        8365.00       +0.25\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       105.95         107.31       +1.28\par  Sing dlr        1.6996         1.6978       -0.11\par  Taiwan dlr      33.692         33.978       +0.85\par  Korean won     1186.00        1192.00       +0.51\par  Baht             38.94          39.59       +1.66\par  Peso             55.46          55.49       +0.05\par  Rupiah         8344.00        8410.00       +0.79.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040116e01g001tk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
