\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Trailing yen as c.banks watch.  \b0\par\par\uc2 521 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 2004\par 03:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Jan 9 (Reuters) - Concerns over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose to the fore once again in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par markets on Friday, keeping the Japanese yen and the rest of the\par regionals steady and seemingly oblivious to the rallying euro.\par  \par     The Singapore dollar        met strong resistance near\par 1.6935 per dollar, an April 2000 peak it matched this week.\par     The Korean won                   was forced off a two-month\par high near 1,181 per dollar by a finance ministry statement.\par     Analysts said this underperformance of many Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the euro and the yen would probably be a\par continuing feature in the early part of 2004.\par     "We continue to hold the view that Asia is going to do well\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 over calendar year 2004 but, in the first quarter and maybe  \f28 \par \par \uc2 even second quarter, we are very nervous about holding long  \par \par \uc2 won, long Thai baht and long Taiwanese dollar positions," said  \par \par \uc2 Michael Jansen, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with National Australia  \par \par \uc2 bank in Sydney.  \par \par \uc2 "There is obviously strong potential for significant  \par \par \uc2 rallies across the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  complex but, at this point in  \par \par \uc2 time, monetary authorities continue to fight more aggressively.  \par \par \uc2 Regional policymakers might be waiting for a clear signal  \par \par \uc2 from China on whether it will allow a more flexible yuan, he  \par \par \uc2 said.  \par \par \uc2 The continuing underperformance expected across Asia called  \par \par \uc2 for a medium-term long yen position against some of the  \par \par \uc2 regionals such as won, he added.  \par \par \uc2 Since early December, the euro has risen about six percent  \par \par \uc2 against the dollar but the yen has risen only about 3.6  \par \par \uc2 percent. That compares with a two percent rally in the Sing  \par \par \uc2 dollar and won and a 1.5 percent in the Taiwan dollar .   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Rising stock markets across the region did little to boost\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Indonesian rupiah        posted token gains against the\par dollar with election uncertainty undermining the unit, while\par the Philippine peso  struggled to rise.\par     The Thai baht        was listless around 39 per dollar,\par having come off Wednesday's highs around 38.93.\par     Analysts said the Sing dollar was slightly into the weaker\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 side of the undisclosed trade-weighted band it's managed in, so  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 monetary authorities were unlikely to be too disturbed by its  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 gains.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0237 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       106.15         106.14       -0.01\par  Sing dlr        1.6933         1.6951       +0.11\par  Taiwan dlr      33.785         33.797       +0.04\par  Korean won     1182.10        1182.40       +0.03\par  Baht             38.98          38.98       +0.00\par  Peso             55.