\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Dn Late On Suspected BOJ, MAS  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 582 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 2004\par 09:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was lower late Friday after suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities pushed the U.S. dollar higher against the yen and other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Some Singapore banks also bought U.S. dollars - speculated to be at the behest of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  - while the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was believed to be taking place in the afternoon, a trader said.  \par \par \uc2 Around 0800 GMT, the U.S. unit was quoted at S$1.6968, higher than S$1.6962 around the same time Thursday. It traded an intraday range of S$1.6935-S$1.6980.  \par \par \uc2 "It's all dollar-yen," said a dealer from a U.S. bank. He said pre-Lunar New Year demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and expected Singapore-dollar purchases to pay for Temasek Holding's S$2.1 billion offering of SingTel shares and exchangeable notes weren't major factors Friday, unlike earlier in the week.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to a four-year low of S$1.6935 earlier in the session, in line with a broad U.S. dollar weakness against regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but bounced back up to its session high of S$1.6980 by mid-afternoon.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the U.S. dollar was traded at Y107.01 late in Asia. It had surged from around Y106.15 early Friday to as high as Y108.29 as Japanese authorities reportedly spent US$3 billion-US$5 billion to buy dollars.  \par \par \uc2 Looking ahead, the U.S. bank dealer said the Singapore dollar would likely continue to track the yen ahead of U.S. employment data due later in the global day, keeping to a S$1.6935-S$1.6990 range.  \par \par \uc2 Singapore government bonds were slightly higher Friday, outperforming U.S. Treasurys that ended mostly flat in Asia.  \par \par \uc2 "A strong Sing dollar and expectations for money market rates to remain low" are shoring local bond prices despite the rising stock market and improving economic outlook, a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 Another dealer said the outlook for local bonds next week will depend on external factors.  \par \par \uc2 "It's anybody's guess - there're U.S. Treasurys, (U.S.) jobless data, (and) dollar/yen to look at," the dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 Over the longer period, Singapore government bond yields are expected to o  \par \par \uc2 At the end of Friday's session, the yield on the two-year bonds was down at 1.02% from 1.03% Thursday. The yield on the 10-year bond was also one basis point lower at 3.64%, while the 15-year bond yield fell two basis points to 4.07%.  \par \par \uc2 Interest rate swaps also fell slightly, in line with lower bond yields, with the two-year swap offered at 1.69% from 1.70% previously; the five-year swap at 2.99% from 3.01%; and the 10-year swap at 4.09% from 4.10%.  \par \par \uc2 The spread between two- and 10-year swaps was unchanged at 240 basis points.  \par \par \uc2 Rates were mixed in the local money market with the overnight interbank rate rising to 0.6250% from 0.5625% Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Prices quoted in this report are pre-settlement bids obtained from dealers and are subject to change. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg}}}\par \par \uc2 -By Kevin Lim, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4150; kevin.lim@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040109e0190009j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
