\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Up Late; Foreigners Build US Dlr Shorts  \b0\par\par\uc2 574 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 2004\par 09:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar climbed higher in Asia Thursday as foreign investment houses continued to build U.S. dollar short positions amid overall bearish sentiment toward the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 But the U.S. unit's slide was limited by Singapore dollar selling from local banks, possibly on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 While players remain wary of more potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the coming sessions, the U.S. unit's dire weakness could again push the U.S. dollar to a fresh multiyear low against its Singaporean counterpart.  \par \par \uc2 Just Wednesday in New York, the U.S. dollar fell to a new four-year low of S$1.6935, mainly owing to its plunge to a fresh 40-month low against the yen - sliding under Y106.00 for the first time since September 2000.  \par \par \uc2 With the U.S. dollar-Singapore dollar pair still bearish in the medium term, the U.S. unit is likely to continue drifting lower toward strong support at S$1.6910 over the next few days, said United Overseas Bank in a research report.  \par \par \uc2 At 0755 GMT Thursday, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.6962, down from S$1.6979 Wednesday in Singapore. Intraday, it traded between S$1.6954 and S$1.6982.  \par \par \uc2 Prices of Singapore government bonds rose in the session, especially in the short-end of the curve, on strong buying by market participants.  \par \par \uc2 A few players, fearful of a better-than-expected U.S. employment report Friday, shifted out of long-term Singapore government bonds into shorter-dated bonds, steepening the yield curve slightly.  \par \par \uc2 "We saw some switching into three and four-year (maturities) out of the long end," said a Singapore dealer.  \par \par \uc2 But, long-dated Singapore government bonds were also relatively firm, supported by decent buying from investors, dealers added.  \par \par \uc2 Given vague notions that December's non-farm payrolls could beat expectations, those market players preferred to hold Singapore government bonds with short durations.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. non-farm payrolls are likely to be a key focus for the Singapore government bond market's future direction. Analysts' forecasts center on a rise in non-farm payrolls of 150,000 and an unchanged unemployment rate of 5.9%.  \par \par \uc2 At the end of the session, the yield on the two-year bonds had fallen three basis points to 1.03%. The yield on the 10-year bond had dropped three basis points to 3.66%, while the 15-year bond yield moved down two basis points to 4.08%.  \par \par \uc2 The two-year interest rate swap declined six basis points to 1.70%, while the five-year swap was offered five basis points lower at 3.01%. The 10-year offer ended six basis points lower at 4.10%.  \par \par \uc2 The spread between two- and 10-year swaps widened to 240 basis points from 230 basis points late Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 In the local money market, rates were mostly steady, with the overnight interbank rate rising to 0.5625% from 0.3125% Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Prices quoted in this report are pre-settlement bids obtained from dealers and are subject to change. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg}}}\par \par \uc2 -By Ron Harui, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4150; ron.haruidowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Simon Harvey  \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040108e0180008x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
