\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Strong but wary on euro's retreat.  \b0\par\par\uc2 680 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 2004\par 04:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Jan 7 (Reuters) - Asian regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were\par mostly higher on Wednesday, but suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the U.S. dollar's recovery from record lows\par against the euro were expected to cap gains.\par     The Singapore dollar        was firm but off the fresh\par 44-month peak of 1.6951 per dollar it had hit in offshore trade\par overnight. The South Korean won             was off a\par three-week high of 1,186.4 it had touched on Tuesday.\par     The Taiwan dollar          and Thai baht        rose to\par their strongest since the middle of October at 33.78 and 39.06\par respectively, before coming off.\par     The Indonesian rupiah        was steady at around 8,335, a\par level not traded since July. The Philippine peso  tested\par 55 per dollar, its highest in two months. The peso has not\par traded on the stronger side of the 55 level since October.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said investors and speculators were watching the\par euro's retreat from Tuesday's record high of $1.2812, to judge\par if there was scope for a larger correction of the European\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent sharp rise against the U.S. dollar.\par  \par     A correction in the euro would put a halt to gains in Asian\par regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , they said.\par     CORRECTION RISK\par     Peter Redward, strategist at Deutsche Bank in Singapore,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said that was a risk, but it was not clear if the euro was  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 taking a temporary breather or was at the start of a big  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 retracement.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It is a tough question to answer. The market is too  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 bullish and is relatively long (on the euro), so there is a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 possibility of a sharp correction," he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Redward said after an almost linear rise, the euro could  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ease to around $1.2550 and the yen could fall to around  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 107 to the dollar, moves that could push the Singapore dollar  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 back to the weaker side of 1.7000, the Korean won to 1,195 and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the Taiwan dollar to 33.90.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "But so far it seems like a very shallow correction and is\par likely to be only temporary," he said.\par     Redward said he was not expecting a big retracement of\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains, even if the euro undergoes a large\par correction, because the regionals had lagged gains in the euro.\par     Dealers said suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Asian central banks,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 directly or through other banks, had not been very aggressive  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 so far. But a U.S. dollar rebound could turn this situation  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 around very quickly, they said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "We have felt the presence of dollar bids from central\par banks all along," said a dealer at a foreign bank in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Bank of Japan has been suspected of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par repeatedly since Monday to stop the yen  from\par appreciating through the 106 per dollar level.\par     Early on Wednesday, the Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold\par HK$4.27 billion in three \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to buy U.S. dollars and\par curb the Hong Kong dollar's  rise.\par     The Hong Kong dollar traded at 7.7628/38, against the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 pegged level of HK$7.80 per dollar. Wednesday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 followed sales of HK$505 million on Monday and HK$4.06 billion  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 on Tuesday.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day 0245 GMT   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       106.32         106.24       -0.08\par  Sing dlr        1.6975         1.6992       +0.10\par  Taiwan dlr      33.825         33.830       +0.01\par  Korean won     1187.50        1187.00       -0.04\par  Baht             39.08          39.16       +0.20\par  Peso             55.11          55.11       +0.00\par  Rupiah         8343.00        8330.00       -0.16\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       106.32         107.01       +0.65\par  Sing dlr        1.6975         1.7014       +0.23\par  Taiwan dlr      33.825         34.050       +0.67\par  Korean won     1187.50        1197.90       +0.88\par  Baht             39.08          39.59       +1.31\par  Peso             55.11          55.50       +0.71\par  Rupiah         8343.00        8460.00       +1.40.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040107e0170015r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
