\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore dlr hits fresh 44-mth highs, baht near 39/dlr.  \b0\par\par\uc2 246 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 2004\par 02:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     0100 - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar        hits fresh 44-month\par highs but fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the\par euro's  retreat from record highs against the U.S. dollar\par could cap further gains, dealers say.\par  \par     - Sing dollar trades around 1.6970 per U.S. dollar, after\par touching 1.6951 in overnight offshore trade.\par     - Sing dollar has been in demand on persistent U.S. dollar\par losses against major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and Singapore's improving\par economic outlook.\par     - But dealers say the euro's sharp pull back from record\par highs of $1.2812 may be the start of an expected correction of\par the U.S. dollar's recent sharp decline.\par     - A correction in the U.S. dollar may put a halt to recent\par gains in Asian regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , said a dealer in Singapore.\par     - The dealer said some Singaporean banks have been buying\par U.S. dollars in recent sessions sparking rumours that\par authorities were trying to curb local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     - The Bank of Japan had been suspected of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par repeatedly since Monday to stop the yen  from\par appreciating through the 106 per dollar level.\par     - Thai baht        rises to 39.10 per dollar level, its\par highest since October 13, in early offshore trade mostly\par supported by invest