\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Strengthen with an eye on central banks.  \b0\par\par\uc2 587 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 2004\par 04:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Jan 6 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strengthened\par on Tuesday, taking their cue from the U.S. dollar's decline\par against the euro and yen, with only the fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  restricting much sharper gains.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar        traded in sight of a 44-month\par peak of 1.6970 per dollar hit on Monday. The Thai baht ,\par Taiwan dollar  and Indonesian rupiah        traded near\par highs last seen in mid-October and the South Korean won\par   touched three-week highs.\par  \par     Asia's worst performer of 2003, the Philippine peso       ,\par hit a one-month high of 55.15 per dollar.\par     Dealers said with the dollar hitting fresh record lows\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against the euro  almost daily, and with the yen\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 just shy of September 2000 highs on the stronger side of the  \par \par \uc2 106 per dollar, Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were set to rise further.  \par \par \uc2 "Right now the overwhelming theme is the overall U.S.  \par \par \uc2 dollar weakness and how does that effect the market place,"  \par \par \uc2 said Simon Flint, Bank of America strategist in Singapore.  \par \par \uc2 With the dollar expected to ease further against major  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in coming weeks, Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  could rise to  \par \par \uc2 stronger levels, he said.  \par \par \uc2 "After all we are living in Asia in a soft dollar peg  \par \par \uc2 environment. The dollar is still the determining factor here,"  \par \par \uc2 he said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the most aggressive players in the market were  \par \par \uc2 offshore investment banks and funds bidding almost all Asian  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "People believe that the U.S. is very happy with the weak  \par \par \uc2 dollar situation and the Europeans and Japanese are not  \par \par \uc2 opposing it sufficiently so until they see things prove  \par \par \uc2 otherwise they are going to continue selling the dollar," Flint  \par \par \uc2 said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar has been in decline since early 2002, as worries  \par \par \uc2 have grown about a gap between U.S. savings and investments and  \par \par \uc2 exports and imports. Analysts say the market suspects the  \par \par \uc2 United States has shifted to an undeclared policy of allowing  \par \par \uc2 the dollar to weaken to help adjust those imbalances.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said U.S. dollar purchases by some local or  \par \par \uc2 state-run banks in Singapore, Thailand, Taiwan and Korea early  \par \par \uc2 on Tuesday had raised suspicion that central banks were trying  \par \par \uc2 to manage the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains.  \par \par \uc2 Aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Japan, suspected to  \par \par \uc2 have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday, to curb the yen's rise through the  \par \par \uc2 106 level, could put a halt to gains in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "But if the 106 level is taken, we can see much sharper  \par \par \uc2 gains (in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) from here," said a dealer at a  \par \par \uc2 European bank in Singapore.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  \par \par \uc2 Change on the day 0314 GMT   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       106.14         106.96       +0.77\par  Sing dlr        1.6983         1.7003       +0.12\par  Taiwan dlr      33.825         33.900       +0.22\par  Korean won     1187.70        1192.00       +0.36\par  Baht             39.19          39.33       +0.36\par  Peso             55.16          55.27       +0.19\par  Rupiah         8346.00        8388.00       +0.50\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       106.13         107.01       +0.83\par  Sing dlr        1.6983         1.7014       +0.18\par  Taiwan dlr      33.825         34.050       +0.67\par  Korean won     1187.70        1197.90       +0.86\par  Baht             39.20          39.59       +0.99\par  Peso             55.15          55.50       +0.63\par  Rupiah         8339.00        8460.00       +1.45.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040106e01600164\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
