\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Up Late But Rumored MAS Action Curbs Gains  \b0\par\par\uc2 509 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 2004\par 09:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar rose against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday on buying by foreign players, though it later curbed those gains on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 European investment banks and others bought the Singapore dollar amid heightened U.S. dollar bearishness, following the greenback's persistent losses against regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Monday.  \par \par \uc2 But their efforts consistently ran into a wall of U.S.-dollar bids placed around S$1.6970-S$1.6990 by domestic banks, which some dealers speculated may have been on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 While these bids should place a floor under the U.S. dollar-Singapore dollar pair in that range for the rest of the global session, dealers said the pair could fall further to S$1.6900 by the end of this month.  \par \par \uc2 Given the weekend comments by Federal Reserve Governor Ben Bernanke that the chances of a U.S. dollar crisis are "quite low" and that interest rates are likely to stay low for some time, the U.S. unit faces a further downside risk against most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0828 GMT, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.6997, down from S$1.7002 Monday in Singapore. Intraday, it traded between S$1.6970 and S$1.6999.  \par \par \uc2 Prices of Singapore government bonds rose Tuesday as some institutions bought bonds in a buy-and-hold strategy, while other participants bought them to cover short positions, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The medium-to-long-end of the bond curve was especially popular among market players, with yields falling roughly eight basis points for five- to seven-year maturities and dropping 10-15 basis points for 10- to 15-year maturities.  \par \par \uc2 Singapore government bonds should remain firm in the near future amid what dealers consider to be relatively low supply of new issues coming out this year.  \par \par \uc2 At the end of the session, the yield on the two-year Singapore government bonds had fallen four basis points to 1.06%. The yield on the 10-year bond had declined 16 basis points to 3.69%, while the 15-year bond yield moved down 11 basis points to 4.06%.  \par \par \uc2 The two-year interest rate swap dropped eight basis points to 1.76%, while the five-year swap was offered 10 basis points lower at 3.03%. The 10-year offer ended 10 basis points lower at 4.12%.  \par \par \uc2 The spread between two- and 10-year swaps narrowed to 236 basis points from 238 basis points late Monday.  \par \par \uc2 In the local money market, rates were mostly steady, with the overnight interbank rate falling to 0.3750% from 0.4375% Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Prices quoted in this report are pre-settlement bids obtained from dealers and are subject to change. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg}}}\par \par \uc2 -By Ron Harui, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4150; ron.haruidowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040106e0160009z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
