\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Strengthen, c.banks still feared.  \b0\par\par\uc2 729 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2004\par 09:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Jan 5 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar hit a new\par 44-month high on Monday, as most Asian regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strengthened against the U.S. dollar after it fell to fresh\par record lows against the euro.\par     The Singapore dollar        touched 1.6975 per dollar, a\par level not seen since April 2000, before giving up some of the\par gains, but was still on the stronger side of the 1.70 level.\par     The Taiwan dollar          rose to 33.80 per dollar -- its\par highest in about two months -- and the Thai baht  and\par Indonesian rupiah  posted highs not seen since the middle\par of October at 39.30 and 8,388 per dollar respectively.\par  \par     Dealers said offshore players who had kept a low profile\par during the holiday season had returned in an aggressive mood.\par     "What this largely reflects is that investors have come in\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 essentially to the first trading day of the new year and have  \f28 \par \par \uc2 established short dollar/Asia positions," said Peter Redward,  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank in Singapore.  \par \par \uc2 "The central banks have realised that this is a short-term  \par \par \uc2 flow and are allowing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to temporarily strengthen  \par \par \uc2 before they come back and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were at record lows  \par \par \uc2 against the euro. This meant they had weakened on a  \par \par \uc2 trade-weighted basis, and could be pushed higher without fear  \par \par \uc2 of immediate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by regional central banks.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The central banks have been sensitive that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strength would eat into export competitiveness.\par     The trade-weighted weakness was a key trading factor in\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  like the Singapore dollar where authorities manage  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 exchange rate against a trade-weighted basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 with the U.S. dollar, yen and euro as its main components.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLICY REMINDERS  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of Japan to curb  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 recent gains by the yen and similar action by the  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Taiwan served as reminders that Asian central  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 banks policies have not changed.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Central banks may allow some moderate appreciation in the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 next two, three days but I don't see a trend appreciation  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 here," Redward said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     He said policy makers would be cautious ahead of elections\par in several Asian countries this year.\par     Substantial gains in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would only follow a\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 policy move by China on its yuan , he added. China has so  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 far refused to bow to international criticism that its  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , pegged to the U.S. dollar, is undervalued.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The South Korean won             rose to touch a\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 two-week high at 1,192.0 per dollar, but fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  restricted further gains, dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves rose to a record $155.35  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 billion at the end of December from $150.34 billion a month  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 before, helped by a surge in the dollar value of euro  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 denominated assets, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A Reuters poll of 10 dealers found they expected the won to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 move between 1,188.1/1,199.0 this week, with pressure to firm  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 coming from inflows of stock funds by foreign investors and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 hopes for a peaceful resolution to the North Korean nuclear  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 row.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine peso rose to 55.26 per dollar, from  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 last week's lows around 55.50, before giving up some of those  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 gains as news broke that authorities in Manila were checking a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 suspected case of SARS.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dealers in Manila said the peso was helped by some residual  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 year-end remittances from overseas Filipinos.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0810 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       106.96         106.