\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Strong, Sing dlr touches 44-month peak.  \b0\par\par\uc2 816 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2004\par 04:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Jan 5 (Reuters) - Asian regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strengthened against the U.S. dollar early on Monday as the\par American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell to fresh record lows against the euro.\par     The Singapore dollar        touched a 44-month high of\par 1.6975 per dollar, the Taiwan dollar  rose to 33.903 --\par its highest in about two months -- and the Thai baht  and\par Indonesian rupiah  posted highs not seen since\par mid-October at 39.35 and 8,424 per dollar respectively.\par     However against the euro, most regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were at\par record lows. Dealers said that meant they had weakened on a\par trade-weighted basis, and could be pushed higher without the\par fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by regional central banks' who had been\par sensitive that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength would eat into export\par competitiveness.\par     Dealers said offshore players who had kept a low profile\par during the holiday season, seemed to have returned in an\par aggressive mood.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "So expect to see continued substantial further\par appreciation," said James Malcolm, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at JP\par Morgan Chase in Singapore.\par     "Prerequisites will be continued global growth which feeds\par through into some domestic demand indicators which is already\par happening to some extent," he said.\par     Dealers said major funds and investment banks that keep an\par eye on the trade-weighted value of Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , sold\par dollar/Asia crosses to reflect the greenback's decline against\par major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     EYES ON TRADE-WEIGHTED VALUE\par     The U.S. dollar's plunge in recent sessions to record lows\par against the euro  and three-year troughs against the yen\par   has pulled its trade-weighted value        to its\par weakest in about seven years.\par  \par     Analysts say Asian central banks keep a close watch on the\par trade-weighted value of their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Singapore manages its dollar against a trade-weighted\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of trade partners. Although the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 constituents and their weights in that basket are a secret,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 analysts believe the U.S. dollar, yen and euro are its major  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 components.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar has been in a trend decline since early 2002, as  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 worries grow on the gap between U.S. savings and investments  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 and exports and imports.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts say the market suspects United States has shifted  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to an undeclared policy of allowing the dollar to weaken and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 help adjust those imbalances.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve Governor Ben Bernanke said on Sunday he did  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 not see much chance of a "dollar crisis" developing in which  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's value kept plunging lower.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He also said that while the U.S. economy appears to have  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 turned a corner, after a slowdown, the Fed would continue to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 hold interest rates at 45-year lows given the low rate of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 inflation.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "The comments this morning from Bernanke obviously gave the\par euro the fresh leg up," Malcolm said.\par     "That sort of continues to reiterate from all sides that\par policy makers are not particularly concerned at the moment\par (about the dollar's decline)," he said.\par     He said Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had so far lagged appreciation\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 seen in other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the dollar, although the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 region's fast improving economic fundamentals suggested that  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 they should have led the move.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The South Korean won             was a touch higher\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 at 1,194.10 per dollar as fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 kept it capped, dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves rose to a record $155.35  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 billion at the end of December from $150.34 billion a month  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 before, helped by a surge in the dollar-converted value of euro  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 denominated assets, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A Reuters poll of 10 dealers found they expected the won to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 move between 1,188.1/1,199.0 this week, with pressure to firm  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 coming from inflows of stock funds by foreign investors and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 hopes for a peaceful resolution to the North Korean nuclear  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 row.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine peso rose to touch 55.37 per dollar,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 from last week's lows around 55.50, before news broke that  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 authorities in Manila were checking a suspected case of SARS.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day 0320 GMT \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       106.93         106.89       -0.04\par  Sing dlr        1.6994         1.7017       +0.14\par  Taiwan dlr      33.914         33.976       +0.18\par  Korean won     1194.10        1195.00       +0.08\par  Baht             39.33          39.59       +0.66\par  Peso             55.40          55.50       +0.18\par  Rupiah         8425.00        8436.00       +0.13\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       106.93         106.91       -0.02\par  Sing dlr        1.6994         1.7006       +0.07\par  Taiwan dlr      33.914         33.978       +0.19\par  Korean won     1194.10        1192.60       -0.13\par  Baht             39.33          39.60       +0.69\par  Peso             55.40          55.55       +0.27\par  Rupiah         8425.00        8460.00       +0.42.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040105e0150010j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
