\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Up Late; Edges Near Key S$1.7000 Intraday  \b0\par\par\uc2 551 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 2003\par 10:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar rose slightly against the U.S. unit in Asia Tuesday on light corporate demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of the New Year holidays.  \par \par \uc2 While the Singapore dollar edged up toward the psychologically key level of S$1.7000 against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore may buy the greenback capped the Singapore dollar's rise.  \par \par \uc2 At 0825 GMT, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7015, down from S$1.7042 late Monday in Asia. It traded between S$1.7010 and S$1.7025 intraday.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar opened around S$1.7022 in Singapore and drifted lower as some banks sold U.S. dollars for Singapore dollars to fulfill the year-end demand from commercial customers.  \par \par \uc2 But concerns that the MAS would step in to prevent an excessive U.S. dollar fall - which would hurt the republic's exports, the main engine of its nascent economic recovery - curbed its decline, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 In recent sessions, the MAS is suspected to have been quietly stepping into the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to smooth the U.S. dollar's slide against the Singapore dollar, making most players wary of testing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's resolve, the dealers added.  \par \par \uc2 For the rest of the week, potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to keep the U.S. dollar above S$1.7000, although underlying U.S. dollar bearishness and improving domestic economic fundamentals could push the U.S. unit below that level early next year.  \par \par \uc2 "I'm targeting S$1.6600 by the middle of next year," said a Singapore dealer.  \par \par \uc2 Prices of Singapore government bonds drifted lower in Asia in the wake of U.S. Treasurys' fall overnight, but most market participants refrained from trading actively ahead of the New Year holidays.  \par \par \uc2 After Wednesday's half-day session, Singapore's government bond market will be closed until Jan. 2.  \par \par \uc2 Singapore government bond yields were slightly higher across the curve, but further swings in yields may be limited as overall trading could be subdued until next week, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At the end of the session, the yield on two-year government bonds was unchanged at 1.01%. The yield on the 10-year bond rose three basis points to 3.75%, while the 15-year yield gained two basis points to close at 4.05%.  \par \par \uc2 The two-year interest rate swap was two basis points higher at 1.73%, while the five-year swap rose four basis points to 2.98%. The 10-year offer ended four basis points higher at 4.06%.  \par \par \uc2 The spread between two- and 10-year swaps widened to 233 basis points from 231 basis points late Monday.  \par \par \uc2 In the local money market, rates were mostly steady, though the overnight interbank rate slipped to 0.3750% versus 0.4375% late Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Prices quoted in this report are pre-settlement bids obtained from dealers and are subject to change. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg}}}\par \par \uc2 -By Ron Harui, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4150; ron.harui@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Dawn Lye  \par \par \uc2 1