\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Preparing for strength in 2004.  \b0\par\par\uc2 663 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 2003\par 08:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE, Dec 29 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were a mixed\par bunch on Monday as the Japanese yen's fickle-mindedness and\par economic data kept them from settling down in holiday-thinned\par trading.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar        first fell as fears of Japanese\par dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lifted the U.S. dollar off lows, but\par recovered as geopolitical worries and concerns over the U.S.\par current account deficit resurfaced to undermine the U.S. dollar\par once again.\par     The Sing dollar was close to last Friday's highs of 1.7023\par in afternoon trade and the Korean won             too\par rallied off one-month lows as markets took the yen back up to\par 107 per dollar.\par     "Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remain bid as strong data coupled with\par good stock market performance prepare the market for another\par strong year," BNP Paribas' \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst Thio Chin Loo said.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The Sing dollar is seeking new highs as the year closes,\par and we expect the Sing dollar to move below 1.7000 when the new\par year begins."\par     Thailand on Monday forecast a robust 8.3 percent GDP growth\par next year, after an expected 6.4 percent in 2003, and also\par forecast an over 14 percent export growth in 2004.\par  \par     But Korean data disappointed markets as the industrial\par output fell in November from October.\par     As the yen rallied past 107 and South Korean stocks\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 recovered, markets shed their worries about the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 wanting to keep the won weak for end-of-year accounting and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 pushed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from 1,201 up to 1,198 per dollar.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The won is among the few Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to have fallen  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 against the U.S. dollar in 2003, beleaguered by Korea's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 consumer debt problems, including accounting irregularities at  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SK Global Co (01740.KS) and the recent cash crunch at LG Card  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Co , and the anxiety over North Korea's nuclear  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ambitions.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Thai baht was stable around 39.60 per dollar.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After rising nearly nine percent against the dollar this year,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the baht is one of Asia's best performers after the yen.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Little reaction was seen to news of a suspected SARS case  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in China as traders braced for more U.S. dollar weakness at the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 start of 2004.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The exception was the Philippine peso . Among Asia's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 weakest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in 2003, the peso was set for more weakness  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 from seasonal factors and political worries heading into  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 presidential elections early next year.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "There is no aggressive position-taking from here on, but  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the medium term bias may tilt towards more gradual weakening of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the peso," said Rovic De Guzman, the head of trading at the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Union Bank of the Philippines.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The peso opened steady after a week of holidays  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 around 55.53 to 55.60 per dollar. It bounced off an all-time  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 low of 55.85 per dollar on November 27, but markets have  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 remained jumpy.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I won't be surprised to see the market retest historical  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 peso lows in the near term," De Guzman said, adding the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 seasonal inflows from expatriate Filippinos at the end of the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 year was starting to wane.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0740 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       107.01         106.99       -0.02\par  Sing dlr        1.7038         1.7048       +0.06\par  Taiwan dlr      34.060         34.050       -0.03\par  Korean won     1197.90        1199.80       +0.16\par  Baht             39.57          39.56       -0.03\par  Peso             55.55          55.59       +0.07\par  Rupiah         8475.00        8485.00       +0.12\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       107.01         118.74      +10.96\par  Sing dlr        1.7038         1.7341       +1.78\par  Taiwan dlr      34.060         34.753       +2.03\par  Korean won     1197.90        1185.80       -1.01\par  Baht             39.57          43.08       +8.87\par  Peso             55.55          53.38       -3.91\par  Rupiah         8475.00        8940.00       +5.49.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031229dzct001sy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
