\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Anxious about SARS and  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 362 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 2003\par 03:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Dec 19 (Reuters) - Fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and a recurrence of the SARS epidemic weighed on\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Friday, keeping them steady to slightly\par weak.\par  \par     Besides, the U.S. dollar was steady after hitting a fresh\par low against the euro overnight, its 13th in 15 sessions.\par     The Singapore dollar was sold in early trade after reports\par of five ill people among 75 quarantined in Singapore for coming\par into contact with a Taiwan researcher who has SARS.\par     Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome (SARS) struck Asia and\par Canada early this year, killing about 800 people and hurting\par economies.\par     In South Korea, as in Japan, traders were worried about\par central banks stepping in to curb \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains.\par     "Most people believe Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will strengthen in\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2  2004 especially against the soft dollar and I am positioned for   \par \par \uc2  that view," said David Simmonds, markets strategist with the   \par \par \uc2  Royal Bank of Scotland.   \par \par \uc2  "But over the next couple of weeks or so I think the risk   \par \par \uc2  is that we have a little pop the other way and dollar/Asia goes   \par \par \uc2  up a bit into the new year."   \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar opened weak at 34.06 to the U.S. dollar,   \par \par \uc2  with markets there still worried about the SARS case, the   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The Singapore dollar met resistance around 1.7050 in\par offshore deals and was a quarter cent weaker.\par     "The risk is to the upside in dollar/Sing. People are\par showing some buying interest," said one Singapore-based trader.\par     The Indonesian rupiah was also slightly weaker with traders\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reporting buying of dollars by importers. It had been supported\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par this week by expectations of a $339 inflow from the Indonesian\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank Restructuring Agency's sale of a large stake in PT Bank\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The won straddled 1,190, keeping to the weaker side of the\par narrow band it has traded in most of this week.\par     "There is still a pretty determined \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  effort\par going on by word and by deed," Simmonds said of Korea.\par     "On a very short-term perspective, it is certainly enough\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to discourage too much supply of dollars. The market is not\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par being allowed to go lower."\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031219dzcj000bg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
