\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -C.bank fear, stocks sell-off cap gains.  \b0\par\par\uc2 712 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2003\par 09:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Dec 16 (Reuters) - Suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by\par central banks and a stock market sell-off restricted gains in\par most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Tuesday, despite the U.S. dollar's\par fall to new lows against the euro.\par     The U.S. dollar fell to a record low of $1.2340 against the\par euro  and struggled only a touch higher from four-session\par lows against the yen .\par     The South Korean won fell from a three-week high on what\par dealers in Singapore said was aggressive U.S. dollar buying by\par state-run banks that sparked rumours of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The won                   fell more than half a percent to\par a four-session low of 1,190.6 per dollar from Monday's high of\par 1,182.8. Dealers said a sell-off in the Korean stock market,\par amid worries about ailing credit card firm LG Card Co\par  , further weighed on the won.\par     The Taiwan dollar          was hit by suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  U.S. dollar bids, as it rose near a one-week high at the\par 34 per U.S. dollar level.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Dealers said U.S. dollar sales by\par exporters still kept the Taiwan dollar's downside limited.\par     There were also worries about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par where the local dollar  rose to 1.7070 per U.S. dollar, a\par level not seen since May 2000.\par     Jimmy Koh, head of research at Singapore's UOB Bank, said\par on a trade-weighted basis the Sing dollar had not appreciated\par to the extent where authorities might step in.\par     "The Sing dollar's rise is very much in line with the U.S.\par dollar's weakness," he said, adding that if the dollar\par continued to decline the Sing dollar could hit 1.7000.\par     Based on his calculations, he said the Sing dollar was\par still 0.8 to 1.0 percent to the weaker side from the mid-point\par of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's trade-weighted policy band.\par     Koh said the U.S. dollar was in a long-term decline, given\par the large gap between U.S. savings and investments, and only\par action by the world's major central banks would stop its fall\par in the short term.\par     He said either the Bank of Japan would need to step in to\par pull the yen down, or European companies would have to make\par enough noise to spark a response from their governments.\par     On Monday, the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Chief Economist Otmar\par Issing said the ECB could \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets if it\par felt the need to.\par     For now, dealers said, improving Asian economic data would\par keep players looking for opportunities to build fresh short\par U.S. dollar positions and bid regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  higher.\par     Data from Singapore on Monday showed retail sales in\par October rose 6.4 percent over September and 13.9 percent over\par the year to October. The rise was above a median market\par expectation of a 3.2 percent increase on the month and 11.8\par percent from a year earlier.\par  \par     No