\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -C.bank suspicions halt early gains.  \b0\par\par\uc2 640 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2003\par 04:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Dec 16 (Reuters) - The South Korean won fell\par from a three-week high early on Tuesday, while other Asian\par regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  took heart from the dollar's overnight fall\par to record lows against the euro and a firmer Japanese yen.\par     The U.S. dollar fell to a record low of $1.2323 against the\par euro  and to four-session lows against the yen        in\par New York trade, before recouping some of those losses.\par     Dealers in Singapore said aggressive U.S. dollar buying by\par state-run banks early on Tuesday spurred talk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and pulled the won             down by about\par half a percent from Monday's high of 1,182.8.\par     They said a sell off in the Korean stock market, amid\par worries about ailing credit card firm LG Card Co ,\par further weighed on the won.\par     The Taiwan dollar          also met resistance from\par suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  U.S. dollar bids, as it rose to a near\par one-week high at the 34 per U.S. dollar level.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Dealers said the\par Taiwan dollar was bid higher by U.S. dollar sales from\par exporters.\par     There were also worries about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par where the local dollar  rose to 1.7070 per U.S. dollar, a\par level not seen since May 2000.\par     Peter Redward, strategist at Deutsche Bank in Singapore,\par said central banks would continue to resist \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par appreciation, to protect exports, as long as there were doubts\par about the sustainability of the U.S. and global economic\par recovery.\par  \par     "There is only one issue in the market right now and that\par is how sustainable is the recovery in the U.S.," he said.\par     Redward said so far economic data from the U.S. had been in\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 line with or above expectations. However, the recent  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 performance of the U.S. stock market suggest investors were  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 still worried about downside risks, he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investor worries include a weakening dollar, fears of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 terrorism, U.S. trade tensions, a huge gap between U.S. savings  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 and investments and the petering out of fiscal and monetary  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 stimuli.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For now, dealers said, improving Asian economic data would  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 keep players looking for opportunities to build fresh short  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. dollar positions and bid regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  higher.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Data from Singapore on Monday showed retail sales in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 October rose 6.4 percent over September and 13.9 percent over  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the year to October. The rise was above a median market  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 expectation of a 3.2 percent increase on the month and 11.8  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 percent from a year earlier.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     November non-oil exports data due on Wednesday were also\par expected to show a continued strong performance.\par     The Thai baht        edged a touch lower against the\par dollar, from late Monday's 39.63, but was well within its\par recent 39.60-39.80 trading range.\par     The Philippine peso        fell to its lowest in about two\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 weeks, pressed by local corporate demand for U.S. dollars.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0255 GMT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     107.75         108.00       +0.23\par  Sing dlr      1.7073         1.7090       +0.10\par  Taiwan dlr    34.015         34.028       +0.04\par  Korean won   1188.30        1182.80       -0.46\par  Baht           39.64          39.62       -0.05\par  Peso           55.50          55.49       -0.02\par  Rupiah       8488.00        8475.00       -0.15\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     107.75         118.74      +10.20\par  Sing dlr      1.7073         1.7341       +1.57\par  Taiwan dlr    34.015         34.753       +2.17\par  Korean won   1188.30        1185.80       -0.21\par  Baht           39.64          43.08       +8.68\par  Peso           55.50          53.38       -3.82\par  Rupiah       8488.00        8940.00       +5.33.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031216dzcg000p6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
