\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Steady Late; Yen  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Speculation  \b0\par\par\uc2 545 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2003\par 09:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was barely changed late in Asia Thursday after market participants resisted taking positions because of speculation the Bank of Japan had been in the market to support the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Trade was further muted locally on talk the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore may also have acted through local banks to stem the recent appreciation in the Singapore dollar.  \par \par \uc2 At 0830 GMT, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7142, little changed from S$1.7140 late Wednesday. It traded between S$1.7130 and S$1.7144 intraday.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar opened around S$1.7140 and spent most of the session hovering between S$1.7130 and S$1.7140, as banks refrained from active trading.  \par \par \uc2 Speculation that the Bank of Japan had bought U.S. dollars from Wednesday to prevent the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from sliding further against the yen, kept participants, even in Singapore, out of the market.  \par \par \uc2 Near the end of the Asian session, the U.S. dollar was at Y108.24, almost unchanged from Y108.27 late in New York but above Y107.35 in Tokyo late Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The BOJ's actions coincided with some talk in the local market that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore had also bought U.S. dollars from around S$1.7110 through local banks Wednesday to stem the local unit's recent rise, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 But the overall tone for the U.S. dollar remains generally bearish. That could mean Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , like the Singapore dollar, will chalk up more gains in the near-term, with the yen leading the way, dealers added.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar is expected to stay supported against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through to the end of global trade Friday, keeping to a S$1.7100-S$1.7150 range.  \par \par \uc2 Prices of Singapore government bonds ended mixed Thursday, with few trades carried out in a quiet session as the year-end approaches, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Some local bonds opened slightly higher following an overnight rise in U.S. Treasurys, but the gains were generally limited and volumes thinned out early in the session.  \par \par \uc2 The yield on two-year government bonds ended two basis points lower at 1.14%. Longer bond yields were mixed, with the 10-year yield rising two basis points to 3.94% while the 15-year yield was unchanged at 4.42%.  \par \par \uc2 Interest rate swaps were a touch higher, with the two- and five-year offers both inching up by one basis point, to 1.87% and 3.18%, respectively. The 10-year offer closed one basis point higher at 4.29%.  \par \par \uc2 The spread between two- and 10-year swaps was unchanged at 242 basis points.  \par \par \uc2 In the local money market, rates were mostly steady, though the overnight offer rose to 0.3750% from 0.3125% late Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Prices quoted in this report are pre-settlement bids obtained from dealers and are subject to change. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Izham Ahmad, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-415-4150; izham.ahmad@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Simon Harvey and Ryan Woo  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031211dzcb000c0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
