\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  fears outweigh U.S. weakness.  \b0\par\par\uc2 687 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 2003\par 09:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Dec 9 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  settled\par uneasily in tight ranges on Tuesday, defying the U.S. dollar's\par broad weakness as it plumbed new troughs against the euro, yen\par and sterling.\par     The U.S. dollar extended its downtrend in early European\par trading after being steady in Asian trade ahead of a Federal\par Reserve policy statement.\par     Traders were unquestionably bearish on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , citing\par reasons such as the bulging U.S. current account deficit and a\par report showing OPEC countries had repatriated funds at an\par accelerated pace in the first half of this year.\par     "The trend was for the dollar to fall against the euro,\par aussie and sterling and move quite cautiously against the yen,"\par said one Singapore-based trader.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "That seems to have changed with dollar/yen cutting through\par 107.50 but I can bet every dollar that the regional central\par banks are around, either slowing or stopping their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par     Against the yen's over 2.5 percent rise this month versus\par the dollar, the Sing dollar  has rallied just under a\par percent, the Korean won             has risen around 1.8\par percent and the Taiwan dollar has firmed over 0.8 percent.\par     Regional markets meanwhile waited for news out of Chinese\par Premier Wen Jiabao's four-day visit to the United States, after\par a U.S. government official said President George Bush would\par urge Wen to move the yuan to a free-floating \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     One-year Chinese yuan non-deliverable forwards\par moved slightly showing a greater premium on the yuan and\par factoring in an approximate 4.7 percent rise in the yuan in a\par year. The yuan is effectively pegged in a band around 8.28 per\par U.S. dollar.\par     KOREA'S WORRIED\par     The Korean won                   struggled to get past a\par two-week high of 1,186 per dollar after the finance ministry\par said it would step into the market if required.\par     Traders said Korea had been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  aggressively to\par keep the won weak and authorities had tried to keep it below\par 1,190.\par     "The problem with Korea is it has a two-speed economy where\par the external sector is doing well, but the consumer sector will\par start to recover only in the second half of next year,\par according to their own forecasts," said Claudio Piron, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strategist with Standard Chartered Bank in Singapore.\par  \par     "So they don't want to impede the performance of exports at\par all through any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation."\par     Still, some of the negatives that caused the won's fall\par last month, such as heavy bad loans at credit card firms and\par geopolitical risks, were starting to diminish, Piron said.\par     Meanwhile, a suggestion from the government that $20\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion of South Korea's reserves be diverted to a new agency\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to manage and achieve higher returns was opposed by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par   \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Korea's reserves have risen 20 percent this year to over\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par $150 billion, a big chunk of which analysts say is invested in\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Piron said markets would be watching the moves on this\par proposal, as it could mean a higher won if approved.\par     "If that means cutting back on some of the U.S. Treasury\par holdings, it would mean a firmer Korean won," he said.\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at   0808 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       107.15         107.55       +0.37\par  Sing dlr        1.7108         1.7103       -0.03\par  Taiwan dlr      34.015         34.060       +0.13\par  Korean won     1186.60        1186.10       -0.04\par  Baht             39.83          39.86       +0.08\par  Peso             55.32          55.33       +0.02\par  Rupiah         8491.00        8490.00       -0.01\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       107.15         118.74      +10.82\par  Sing dlr        1.7108         1.7341       +1.36\par  Taiwan dlr      34.015         34.753       +2.17\par  Korean won     1186.60        1185.80       -0.07\par  Baht             39.83          43.08       +8.16\par  Peso             55.32          53.38       -3.50\par  Rupiah         8491.00        8940.00       +5.29.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031209dzc9001pn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
