\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Sing dollar, won up on yen rally.  \b0\par\par\uc2 446 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Dezember 2003\par 04:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Dec 8 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar moved\par closer to its November highs and the Korean won firmed past a\par key resistance on Monday morning, boosted by the yen's rally to\par three-year highs after weaker-than-expected U.S. jobs data.\par     Disappointed with the pace of U.S. job creation in\par November, markets sold the U.S. dollar on Friday. The momentum\par took the yen  to three-year highs on Monday and kept the\par euro  close to its strongest levels.\par     The Singapore dollar        rose to 1.7115/25 per dollar,\par approaching November's three-year highs around 1.7095 at a\par unhurried pace that reflected market worries over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Korean won                   dithered after it rose\par past a key resistance of 1,190 overnight, mimicking the yen's\par reluctance to explore highs beyond 107.50.\par  \par     Stock markets around the region were weak after a fall in\par the U.S. stock market.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But analysts said the yen's renewed strength, after\par spending over a week in a narrow band, was positive for Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "Over the past few weeks, U.S. dollar weakness was\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 reflected mainly through the high yielding commodity \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 and the European exchange rates," Philip Wee of DBS Bank said  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in a note.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "Japan and Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have bucked the trend due to lacklustre\par regional stock markets and unsettling domestic politics."\par     "This asymmetry may change this week, especially after U.S.\par dollar/yen broke its key 108 support last Friday," Wee said.\par     Markets were also on watch for news out of Chinese Premier\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wen Jiabao's four-day visit to the United States, since he is  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 expected to face criticism of China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policies.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0255 GMT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     107.70         108.33       +0.58\par  Sing dlr      1.7123         1.7186       +0.37\par  Taiwan dlr    34.076         34.104       +0.08\par  Korean won   1187.60        1190.90       +0.28\par  Baht           39.87          39.88       +0.03\par  Peso           55.34          55.36       +0.04\par  Rupiah       8493.00        8500.00       +0.08\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     107.70         118.74      +10.25\par  Sing dlr      1.7123         1.7341       +1.27\par  Taiwan dlr    34.076         34.753       +1.99\par  Korean won   1187.60        1185.80       -0.15\par  Baht           39.87          43.08       +8.05\par  Peso           55.34          53.38       -3.54\par  Rupiah       8493.00        8940.00       +5.26.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031208dzc8000jh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichg