\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Unexcited by U.S. dollar descent.  \b0\par\par\uc2 734 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 2003\par 05:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Dec 4 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were\par marginally firmer on Thursday morning, seemingly unimpressed by\par the sliding U.S. dollar and unwilling to test the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par habits of regional central banks.\par     The U.S. dollar was near record lows against the euro\par   and just off a five-year trough against sterling       ,\par undermined by weak sentiment and persisting anxiety over the\par U.S. current account deficit and the Iraq violence.\par     But the yen        bounced off two-week lows near 108 per\par dollar as markets got worried the Bank of Japan would cap its\par gains.\par     The Singapore dollar        was near the past week's peaks\par around 1.7150/60 per dollar, the Korean won\par was headed for Wednesday's two-week highs of 1,190 per dollar,\par and the rest of the regionals were slightly higher on the day.\par     Yet, notwithstanding recent improvements in regional\par economic data, market players seemed to be wary of buying the\par regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  aggressively.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     This week's data showed Korean exports soaring and\par Singapore's manufacturing activity expanding for the sixth\par straight month in November.\par     Bhanu Baweja, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with UBS, said the end of\par the year was probably not the right time to be taking up fresh\par bullish positions on Asia.\par     "Based on the recent raft of data globally and within Asia,\par we become more convinced of an eventual move up in Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  versus the U.S. dollar, though it may be early to\par call for that just yet," he said.\par     With portfolio flows no longer as strong as they had been\par and volumes thinning into the year-end, it was also likely that\par dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would become the bigger\par force in markets, he said.\par  \par     "I would be more wary of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in December than at\par any other point in time."\par     "Hence my view that in the short term, you want to be long\par or neutral dollar/Asia and in the long term, you want to be\par short dollar/Asia," Baweja said.\par     Baweja recommended positioning for this eventual Asian\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 appreciation through spreads, such as buying one-month  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar/won non-deliverable forwards (NDFs) and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 selling the six-month forwards.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SING DOLLAR STILL NEUTRAL  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine peso was steadier around 55.27/35,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 off last week's life lows.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yet, markets were nervous about policy instability after  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the decision by film star Fernando Poe Junior to contest next  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 year's presidential elections, finance secretary Jose Camacho's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 resignation and the likelihood of a deterioration in the budget  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 deficit next year.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Taiwan dollar made light gains, in line with  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the won, and the Indonesian rupiah was virtually  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 unchanged.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Despite the Sing dollar's rise, traders said it was merely  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 mirroring the euro's and yen's moves and was still unchanged in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 trade-weighted nominal exchange rate terms. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 managed in an undisclosed trade-weighted band.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders said markets were slightly disappointed with the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dip in the Singapore Purchasing Managers' Index reading for  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 November, despite it being the sixth month of expansion.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But, more than that, the fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would keep markets from pushing  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the Sing dollar towards 1.71, to three-year highs it struck  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 last month.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The data has been good. But the market is not in a hurry  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to move the Sing dollar to the top end of the band," Baweja  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I don't expect the dollar/Sing to do more than 1.71 this  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 year."  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0325 GMT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     108.22         108.62       +0.37\par  Sing dlr      1.7161         1.7188       +0.16\par  Taiwan dlr    34.107         34.115       +0.02\par  Korean won   1192.40        1195.20       +0.23\par  Baht           39.90          39.88       -0.04\par  Peso           55.29          55.38       +0.17\par  Rupiah       8493.00        8487.00       -0.07\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   Latest