\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Philippine peso falls on Camacho resignation.  \b0\par\par\uc2 554 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 November 2003\par 09:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Nov 21 (Reuters) - The Philippine peso fell\par sharply to near a record closing low on Friday after Finance\par Secretary Jose Camacho said he would resign at the end of the\par month.\par     The peso        ended local trading down half a percent\par from Thursday's close at 55.585 per U.S. dollar. This was near\par its early November lows and within striking distance of its\par all-time low of 55.75 per dollar.\par     It has been Asia's weakest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this year, dogged by\par worries over the budget deficit and politics, and this\par development raised the policy uncertainty, analysts said.\par     "I would imagine there will be a little bit of pressure on\par the spot rate, a bit of pressure on the ROP (sovereign bond)\par spreads and little bit of pressure on the domestic bond market\par until things settle down," said John McGowan, treasurer of\par HSBC, Philippines.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "If there's uncertainty it is bound to create some sort of\par pressure locally."\par     Other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also fell on Friday, undermined by\par the violence in Turkey and Iraq, weak equity markets and the\par worry over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by local authorities.\par     The yen's moves were erratic. It benefited from the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar's decline after the suicide bombings in Turkey and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 blasts in Iraq but fear of Japanese dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 weighed.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Korean won             fell as far as 1,198 per\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar in early deals, its weakness exacerbated by recent  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 comments from Korean authorities that they favoured a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 policy that supported exports.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 REFLATION DOUBTS  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Equity markets in the region were mostly weak on Friday  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 too, and analysts said the bombings had merely given traders an  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 excuse to trim their long positions on Asia ahead of the year  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 end.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Equity markets are being challenged, reflation is being  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 challenged and therefore Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  longs are being  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 challenged," said Bhanu Baweja, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with UBS.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Sing dollar was over a cent off Wednesday's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 three-year highs near 1.71 per dollar, with some traders  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 suspecting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 to rein in the rallying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "As you can see from the dollar, from the lack of upside in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the Aussie and from stock markets, the market has begun  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to challenge the reflation theme," Baweja said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "And that's combined with continued \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 authorities continue to believe that exports are the only  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 bastion of support for their economy."  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0830 GMT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     108.89         108.93       +0.04\par  Sing dlr      1.7228         1.7178       -0.29\par  Taiwan dlr    34.045         34.029       -0.05\par  Korean won   1195.30        1191.50       -0.32\par  Baht           39.88          39.89       +0.03\par  Peso           55.59          55.29       -0.53\par  Rupiah       8505.00        8505.00       +0.00\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     108.89         118.74       +9.05\par  Sing dlr      1.7228         1.7341       +0.66\par  Taiwan dlr    34.045         34.753       +2.08\par  Korean won   1195.30        1185.80       -0.79\par  Baht           39.88          43.08       +8.02\par  Peso           55.59          53.38       -3.97\par  Rupiah       8505.00        8940.00       +5.11.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031121dzbl00249\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
