\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Undermined by Turkey blasts, stocks.  \b0\par\par\uc2 443 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 November 2003\par 04:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Nov 21 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were\par modestly weaker on Friday as the bombings in Turkey and fears\par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by central banks kept investors wary.\par     Analysts said Thursday's attacks by suicide bombers in\par Istanbul gave markets the excuse to trim their bullish\par positions in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "Equity markets are being challenged, reflation is being\par challenged and therefore Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  longs are being\par challenged," said Bhanu Baweja, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with UBS.\par     The U.S. dollar recovered against the yen after a brief\par drop on news of the blasts and ahead of a long weekend in\par Japan.\par     The Korean won                   looked vulnerable as it\par hit five-month lows in early deals and got very close to a key\par level at 1,200.\par     Although the Korean authorities said recently they favour a\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy that supports exports, traders believe the Bank\par of Korea will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to sell dollars if the won's descent is\par too rapid.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , barring the listless Thai baht       ,\par were slightly lower and stock markets around the region, with\par the exception of a recovering Korean market , seemed set\par for declines.\par     The Sing dollar        was a cent off Wednesday's\par three-year highs near 1.71 per dollar, with some traders\par suspecting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par to rein in the rallying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at those highs.\par     "As you can see from the dollar, from the lack of upside in\par the Aussie  and from stock markets, the market has begun\par to challenge the reflation theme," Baweja said.\par     "And that's combined with continued \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The\par authorities continue to believe that exports are the only\par bastion of support for their economy."\par     Heading into the end of the year, markets were also paring\par all their risky positions, he said.\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0313 GMT\par  Change on the day\par  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     109.07         108.93       -0.13\par  Sing dlr      1.7211         1.7178       -0.19\par  Taiwan dlr    34.038         34.029       -0.03\par  Korean won   1194.60        1191.50       -0.26\par  Baht           39.89          39.89       +0.00\par  Peso           55.31          55.29       -0.04\par  Rupiah       8538.00        8505.00       -0.39\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     109.07         118.74       +8.87\par  Sing dlr      1.7211         1.7341       +0.76\par  Taiwan dlr    34.038         34.753       +2.10\par  Korean won   1194.60        1185.80       -0.74\par  Baht 