\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Down Late;  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Talk Lifts US Dlr  \b0\par\par\uc2 489 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 November 2003\par 09:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar tumbled to its lowest level in three sessions Friday, pressured by talk the government was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support the U.S. unit.  \par \par \uc2 Market participants said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore was thought to have been buying U.S. dollars in small amounts since it hit a three-year low of S$1.7105 against the Singapore dollar early Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 "They appear to have been in the market over the past few days to keep the (U.S.) dollar above the S$1.7100 level," a trader at a U.S. bank said.  \par \par \uc2 It is MAS policy not to comment on its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market activities.  \par \par \uc2 After opening trading Friday around S$1.7175, the U.S. dollar climbed steadily to an intraday high of S$1.7240 late afternoon.  \par \par \uc2 At 0820 GMT, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at S$1.7230, up from S$1.7185 late Thursday in Asia.  \par \par \uc2 An improving economic outlook has helped make the Singapore dollar one of the region's best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the end of October (up 1.5%).  \par \par \uc2 But further gains will be more difficult to come by in the near term, United Overseas Bank said in a research note.  \par \par \uc2 Next week's scheduled report on October industrial production should confirm the economic recovery is continuing, but "unless the data outperforms spectacularly, it is unlikely to provide a further boost to the Singapore dollar, given that the recent appreciation has probably factored in all the good news for now already," the bank said.  \par \par \uc2 Singapore government bond prices rose modestly across the curve, continuing the three-week rally that has been inspired by recent gains in U.S. Treasurys.  \par \par \uc2 At the end of the session, the yield on two-year Singapore government bonds was down three basis points at 1.12%.  \par \par \uc2 The yield on the five-year bond was down four basis points at 2.83%.  \par \par \uc2 The yields on the seven- and 10-year bonds were each down three basis points at 3.22% and 3.79%, respectively.  \par \par \uc2 The yield on the 15-year bond was down two basis points at 4.40%  \par \par \uc2 Interest rate swaps were also lower, with the two-year offer down four basis points at 1.80%. The five-year offer was at 3.03%, while the 10-year offer was at 4.18%, both down six basis points.  \par \par \uc2 The spread between two- and 10-year swaps narrowed to 232 basis points from 234 basis points late Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Prices quoted in this report are pre-settlement bids obtained from dealers and are subject to change. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Alan Yonan Jr., Dow Jones Newswires; 65 9862-0905; alan.yonan@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Simon Harvey  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031121dzbl000j6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
