\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won weakest on yen drop, stocks.  \b0\par\par\uc2 580 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 2003\par 09:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Nov 20 (Reuters) - The Korean won led the pack\par of falling Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday as the yen's retreat in\par offshore trading and declines in regional stock markets weighed\par on sentiment.\par     The won                   fell over one percent from\par Wednesday and posted its lowest onshore close in nearly five\par months at 1,191.5 per dollar.\par     The Singapore dollar        fell nearly a cent from\par Wednesday's three-year highs above 1.71, notwithstanding\par optimism over recent upbeat growth and retail sales data.\par     Although the yen        and euro        recovered from\par their overnight falls and the dollar fell prey to worries over\par violence in Iraq and the U.S. decision to impose quotas on\par Chinese textile imports, Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  found little support.\par  \par     "In the near term the market will focus on two distinct\par drivers," National Australia Bank said in a commentary.\par     "The first is the degree of capital inflow into the Asian\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 economic region. While this has been very strong in the past  \par \par \uc2 quarter, there are signs that foreign investors are becoming  \par \par \uc2 less enamored with Asian equity assets with the rate of inflow  \par \par \uc2 into Taiwan dropping away sharply," it said.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The second factor was the value of the yen and market\par perceptions of changes to China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regime, it said.\par     "The trend towards a stronger yen has exerted a strong\par gravitational force, but the opposing force has been the yuan\par peg."\par     Stock markets in Singapore, Thailand, Taiwan, Korea and\par Hong Kong were all weak on Thursday.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par     Traders said the won's decline accelerated after the Bank\par of Korea said it favoured a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy that would support\par exports.\par     Elsewhere, analysts suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday to stop the local dollar rising past\par three-year highs around 1.71.\par     The Indonesian rupiah        traded at its lowest this week\par and the Philippine peso , trading in its weakest ranges\par this year, was indifferent and modestly higher.\par     Markets in Thailand waited for an expected upgrade of the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 country's ratings by Moody's Investors Service, although few  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 see the baht reacting much after the recent string of measures  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 imposed to curb offshore positions and speculation.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are pinned by dollar/yen," said Ray\par Farris, markets strategist with Credit Suisse First Boston.\par     "The Thai baht looks increasingly like a at least temporary\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 peg, the Taiwan dollar looks like a peg, and the won has a bit  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 of volatility but they (Korean authorities) are trying very  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 hard to hold on to the current yen/won levels to prevent  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar/won going below 1,175," Farris said.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 