\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -In a bind over U.S. data,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 636 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 2003\par 04:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Nov 6 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  barely moved\par on Thursday morning as growing evidence of higher growth in the\par United States and data pointing to heavy \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par by local authorities put markets in a quandary.\par     The yen        was weaker, having fallen below 110 per\par dollar after another batch of U.S. data pointing to improving\par growth.\par     In Asia, the Indonesian rupiah        and Philippine peso\par  , the two least correlated with the yen, were slightly\par weaker. The rest were unchanged.\par     The Sing dollar        held a 1.7415/25 range and the\par Korean won             was stable around 1,182 per\par dollar.\par     "I think it is a choppy period now with the struggle\par between data coming out of the United States as well as\par elsewhere, and Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Cliff\par Tan, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and interest rates strategist at Citigroup.\par  \par     "We are maintaining our focus to buy Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on\par dips," he said.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Still, it was a period in which traders ought to be\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cautious, Tan said, with market positions still heavily short\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on dollars and recent surprises on the upside in data coming\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par out of Europe, Japan and other parts.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It could be the beginning of a policy tightening cycle too,\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after Australia led with a rate hike on Wednesday and the Bank\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of England expected to do so soon.\par    \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Recent months have been tumultuous for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets,\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par beginning with the September Group of Seven meeting, calling\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for flexible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policies in Asia, to last week's\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par surprisingly reticent report on global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data showed Asian central banks had\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par continued \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  aggressively through October. Japan spent\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par about $25 billion on yen-weakening \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and China's\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reserves rose to over $400 billion.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par James Malcolm, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with JP Morgan, said\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reserve accumulation in a narrow block comprising China, Japan,\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Korea and Taiwan amounted to $58 billion in September and an\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par estimated $54 billion in October, against a 2003 monthly\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par average of $31 billion.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "In terms of Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , growth and recovery continue\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to unfold in Asia so if the dollar rebounds and it is because\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of growth, that has been generally supportive for Asian\par    \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , almost counter-intuitively sometimes," Tan said.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "But \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  politics may remain quite important for the\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Greater China block and may return again in spite of the fact\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that the market has got calmer since Snow's testimony."\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tan said Asian central banks may reduce the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par keep their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weak as they head into better growth in\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2004.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the lack of confidence with the political leadership in\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par some places, such as Korea and Taiwan, could mean those central\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par banks would be cautious about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation for some\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par more time, he said.\par    \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0305 GMT\par    \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     110.06         109.69       -0.34\par  Sing dlr      1.7417         1.7425       +0.05\par  Taiwan dlr    34.018         34.018       +0.00\par  Korean won   1182.10        1182.40       +0.03\par  Baht           39.86          39.87       +0.03\par  Peso           55.26          55.20       -0.11\par  Rupiah       8515.00        8478.00       -0.43\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     110.06         118.74       +7.89\par  Sing dlr      1.7417         1.7341       -0.44\par  Taiwan dlr    34.018         34.753       +2.16\par  Korean won   1182.10        1185.80       +0.31\par  Baht           39.86          43.08       +8.08\par  Peso           55.26          53.38       -3.40\par  Rupiah       8515.00        8940.00       +4.99 ((Editing by\par Sonali Desai; vidya.ranganathan@reuters.com; Reuters Messaging:\par vidya.ranganathan.reuters.com@reuters.net; +65 6870 3090)).\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031106dzb6000up\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
