\par\par \b \uc2 Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mixed Late; Volatility Dominates Session  \b0\par\par\uc2 779 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2003\par 11:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mixed against the dollar Wednesday in a choppy trading session.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened against the New Taiwan dollar, Philippine peso and Indonesian rupiah, while extending its gains versus the South Korean won and Singapore dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The short-covering rally that sent the dollar soaring against Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  a day earlier appeared to have largely run its course in some markets, leaving the U.S. unit vulnerable to renewed selling pressure, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 "The market has once again been caught out looking for a clearout of dollar shorts only to encounter good demand to sell the dollar into rallies," UBS said in a research note.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. President George W. Bush also contributed to some of the dollar's weakness, vowing Tuesday to press China and Japan to allow their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to move freely against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Bush told reporters he will raise the issue with Japanese Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi during a visit Friday to Tokyo and with Chinese officials during an economic summit in Bangkok next week.  \par \par \uc2 The Thai baht recovered from a three-week low in morning trade to finish the Asian session modestly stronger against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Near the end of Asian trading the dollar was quoted at 39.775 baht, down from THB39.970 late Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The baht opened on a weak note following the Bank of Thailand's move Tuesday to introduce further measures to discourage speculators from taking long positions in the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said the initial weakening of the baht after the new rules were unveiled showed that the policy was working.  \par \par \uc2 However, after peaking at THB40.240 in the first hour of trading, the dollar reversed course and proceeded to weaken for the balance of the session.  \par \par \uc2 A trader at a local bank said exporters viewed the dollar's rise above the THB40 level as a good selling opportunity.  \par \par \uc2 The won fell for the second straight session after hitting a 35-month high against the dollar earlier in the week.  \par \par \uc2 An official at South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Economy attributed the won's slide to market players covering "excessive short-positions" in the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at 1,170.5 won, up from KRW1,166.4 late Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Suspected government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed the dollar to a six-week high of KRW1,175.0 in afternoon trading before the rally began showing signs of fatigue.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar's rise against its Singapore counterpart in volatile trading fueled speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Late in Asia the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7375, up from S$1.7360 late Tuesday in Asia. It traded between S$1.7330 and S$1.7470 intraday.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar opened around S$1.7350 and quickly reached its session high of S$1.7470 on buying led mainly by large local banks, sparking speculation they were acting on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent the rest of the session gyrating between S$1.7380 and S$1.7450, with market attention dominated by its moves against the Thai baht, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 A hands-off approach taken by Taiwan's normally \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allowed the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise modestly against its U.S. counterpart.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar ended at NT$33.900, down from NT$34.051 Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Trading volume totaled US$809 million, down from US$1.16 billion in the previous session.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't as active (Wednesday), after its big move yesterday," a dealer at a foreign bank said.  \par \par \uc2 The peso was buoyed by dollar remittance inflows from Filipinos working overseas.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at 54.620 pesos on the Philippine Dealing System, down from PHP54.720 Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Many Filipinos working abroad traditionally increase their repatriation of funds in the fourth quarter to give family members more spending money for Christmas.  \par \par \uc2 The peso will remain vulnerable, however, due to political concerns ahead of the presidential elections in May next year, analysts say.  \par \par \uc2 The rupiah benefited from expectations of capital inflows into the local stock market.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at 8,425 rupiah, down from its close Tuesday at IDR8,450.  \par \par \uc2 The ongoing initial public offering of a 36% stake in Bank Rakyat Indonesia, which is scheduled to close early next month, is expected to attract foreign investors' interest, helping the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 -By Alan Yonan Jr., Dow Jones Newswires; 65 9862-0905; alan.yonan@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Ryan Woo  \par \par \uc2 1136 4250  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031015dzaf000jo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
