\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Fall on US dollar rise, policy caution.  \b0\par\par\uc2 579 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2003\par 06:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Oct 14 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gave up some\par of their recent gains early on Tuesday, prompted by the U.S.\par dollar's rebound against major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and as caution grew\par over authorities' response to further appreciation.\par     Dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said they suspected there was\par aggressive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of Korea and the Taiwan\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Tuesday to pull their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  down to weaker\par levels.\par     Dealers were wary of the Thai baht as well after it fell to\par a one-week low, down from Monday's three-year highs above 39 to\par the dollar, despite Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra saying\par the government had not yet made any decision on whether to use\par tax measures to discourage \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  speculation.\par     Thai Finance Minister Suchart Jaovisidha was quoted on\par Monday as saying Thailand was considering taxing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par transactions to help stem growing speculation on the strong\par baht.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The South Korean won was down to its lowest in three weeks\par compared with Monday's three-year high, and the Taiwan dollar\par fell to its one-week low from a 14-month high.\par  \par     The region-wide swing in sentiment pulled the Singapore\par dollar to its lowest in over two weeks.\par     Dealers said the move in the market has defied general\par bullish expectations ahead of the President George Bush's visit\par to Asia, next week, and the APEC summit in Thailand.\par     Traders had expected Asian central banks to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  less,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 given United States' persistent criticism of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign  \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy of many Asian nations to keep their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 weak.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Even if you're bearish dollar/Asia, which I am, you have  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to except the reality that these central banks are not going to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 look the other way," said David Simmonds, strategist at Royal  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Scotland in Singapore.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Pending a convincing pick up in domestic demand they  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (central banks) are going to remain pretty sensitive to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 exchange rate moves. That certainly does seem clear," he added.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 However, Simmonds said Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  losses could be a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 corrective move within the well established weak U.S. dollar  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 trend, which is unlikely to reverse anytime soon.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "Periodically we're going to get some pretty sharp and\par unpleasant corrections and this is one of them," he said.\par     Elsewhere, the Philippine peso edged off a one-month high\par hit on Monday but dealers in Manila said fresh remittances from\par overseas workers were supporting the peso.\par     Dealers said with the import season having peaked, and\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 overseas workers remitting dollars for the school admission  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 season, the peso was likely to see stronger levels in coming  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 days.   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0355 GMT\par  Change on the day\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     109.13       108.39         -0.68\par  Sing dlr      1.7296       1.7225         -0.41\par  Taiwan dlr    33.771       33.710         -0.18\par  Korean won   1156.40      1147.20         -0.80\par  Baht           39.42        39.20         -0.55\par  Peso           54.55        54.53         -0.04\par  Rupiah       8387.00      8370.00         -0.20\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     109.13       118.74         +8.81\par  Sing dlr      1.7296       1.7341         +0.26\par  Taiwan dlr    33.771       34.753         +2.91\par  Korean won   1156.30      1185.80         +2.55\par  Baht           39.42        43.08         +9.30\par  Peso           54.55        53.38         -2.14\par  Rupiah       8387.00      8940.00         +6.59.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031014dzae000hf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
