\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -New highs on U.S. dollar fall.  \b0\par\par\uc2 687 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2003\par 05:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Oct 8 (Reuters) - Most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose to\par new highs early on Wednesday, following the U.S. dollar's fall\par to fresh lows against major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The South Korean won            hit a 35-month high, the\par Thai baht  set a new three-year high, the Singapore\par dollar  probed fresh four-month peaks and the Taiwan\par dollar  closed in on one-year highs.\par     The baht also received a boost after Standard and Poor's\par upgraded its credit ratings by one notch. The agency also\par upgraded Indonesia and Malaysia. For a detailed story click on\par            .\par     Dealers said the Japanese yen's        rise through the\par psychological barrier of 110 per dollar, to new three-year\par highs, would raise expectations that central banks in the\par region might allow their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to set fresh highs against\par the U.S. dollar as well.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The 110-level was the next line in the sand where people\par had feared that (Japan's) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 ministry of finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would order\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Bank of America's strategist in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par Simon Flint.\par     "With that level broken it means people are adding to their\par short dollar/Asia positions at the moment, so you are beginning\par to see new (U.S. dollar) lows across the region."\par     However, Flint added that Asian central banks would not\par completely stand out of the way of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation and\par would continue to limit the move.\par     Earlier a senior official at South Korea's finance ministry\par told Reuters there had been no change in the government's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy -- a reference to recent dollar-buying\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Korean authorities.\par     Asia's policy to keep \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weak to help boost exports\par has come under increasing criticism from the United States and\par Europe and the focus has been China's yuan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which is\par virtually pegged at around 8.278 per dollar.\par     Chairman of the U.S. Senate Finance Committee, Charles\par Grassley, on Tuesday sent a letter to the Chinese government,\par threatening action unless the country moves to a flexible\par exchange rate and upholds trade commitments.\par     The yuan's one-year non-deliverable forward contract had\par risen to record premium above 5,000 points per U.S. dollar,\par pricing an appreciation of about six and a half percent.\par     The U.S. Treasury Department is scheduled to report on\par Asia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policies to Congress on October 16, ahead of\par President George Bush's appearance at an APEC summit.\par     Dealers said speculation on a move in the yuan has\par intensified ahead of the APEC gathering in Thailand later this\par month, in which the region's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  management policies are\par expected to be raised.\par     Given China is a major trading partner of most Asian\par economies, any move in the yuan, whenever it comes, will be\par matched by other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Such speculation has also spilled over into the Hong Kong\par dollar  market, pushing the two-decade old peg of 7.8 per\par U.S. dollar to strengthen to levels not seen since October\par 1997.\par     Dealers said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  players would still be cautious in\par Korea and Singapore where monetary policy announcements are due\par on Thursday and Friday, respectively.\par  \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0302 GMT\par  Change on the day\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     109.70       110.47         +0.70\par  Sing dlr      1.7207       1.7236         +0.17\par  Taiwan dlr    33.726       33.793         +0.20\par  Korean won   1148.40      1151.10         +0.24\par  Baht           39.15        39.46         +0.79\par  Peso           54.97        55.05         +0.15\par  Rupiah       8368.00      8385.00         +0.20\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     109.70       118.74         +8.24\par  Sing dlr      1.7207       1.7341         +0.78\par  Taiwan dlr    33.793       34.753         +2.84\par  Korean won   1151.10      1185.80         +3.01\par  Baht           39.15        43.08        +10.04\par  Peso           55.05        53.38         -3.03\par  Rupiah       8368.00      8940.00         +6.84\par     For the new Reuters scrolling global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  service please\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par click .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031008dza8000gy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
