\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Baht rallies, but gains worry others.  \b0\par\par\uc2 790 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Oktober 2003\par 11:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Oct 2 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  held a\par stronger bias on Thursday, helped by stock market gains, with\par the Thai baht rallying to a three-year high as a ratings agency\par placed the country on review for possible upgrade.\par     Led by the yen       , Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have strengthened\par in the two weeks since the Group of Seven called for more\par flexibility in exchange rates, although most regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have been wary of bettering the highs they set early\par last week.\par     Dealers said markets were still cautious for any\par dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by their respective central banks,\par amid talk that the Bank of Japan might have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb\par the yen's rise in early trade.\par     Bhanu Baweja, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at UBS in Singapore, said\par Japan's yen policy was an important determinant of how the rest\par of the region would respond to their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Whether or not reduced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from Japan will result\par in reduced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the rest of the region; that is\par theme number one," he said.\par     He said Asian authorities were suspicious of the\par sustainability of export growth, and were thus wary of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par appreciation.\par     "But they might change their reaction as a result of good\par numbers. So we do believe \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will appreciate backed by\par better economic data," he said.\par     Baweja said such a change in attitude was apparent in\par Thailand, where policymakers have shown tolerance to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strength as the economy outperformed most in the region.\par     Moody's Investor Services placed the country's foreign\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ratings on review for possible upgrade on Thursday,\par citing the strength of the economy.\par     On Thursday the baht        rallied over half a percent to\par 39.58 per dollar, its strongest since July 2000, taking its\par year-to-date gains to close to nine percent.\par     Bank of Thailand Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said early\par in the afternoon the bank had not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the\par baht.\par     "Today the baht is strengthening slightly too fast but we\par haven't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  yet," Pridiyathorn told reporters in\par Bangkok.\par     Dealers in Bangkok suspect authorities do step in\par frequently to buy dollars, and said the Bank of Thailand\par probably did on Thursday to smooth out volatility as the baht\par surged.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TALK\par     But elsewhere, worries about dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par capped the South Korea won  and the Taiwan dollar\par  .\par     Equity- and export-related dollar sales kept the won to\par near 1,150 per dollar, a level it has failed to convincingly\par breach in the last week due to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by authorities.\par     Dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said state banks had pulled the won\par down to a near one-week low on Wednesday, a move they suspected\par was on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Data on Thursday showed\par Korean reserves rose by over $5 billion in September to $141.5\par billion.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  players in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , however, braved rumours of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and pushed the local dollar  to\par a four-month high of 1.7227 per U.S. dollar, dealers said.\par  \par     Dealers said the move was exacerbated after stop-loss U.S.\par dollar sell orders kicked in around 1.7250.\par     Dealers said they suspected Wednesday's U.S. dollar\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 purchases by some local and foreign banks were on behalf of the  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore. Some local banks were seen  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 buying dollars on Thursday as the Sing dollar approached  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 four-month highs.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, Indonesia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it was happy for  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the rupiah to remain in the 8,200-8,700 per dollar  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 range.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Governor Burhanuddin Abdullah also said Fitch Ratings would  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 raise its credit ratings on Indonesia in November. Moody's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors Service upped some ratings on Indonesia this week.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dealers in Jakarta said the rupiah rose to touch 8,360 per  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar, its highest since July. It has risen close to seven  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 percent so far this year. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0833  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GMT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     110.96       111.24         +0.25\par  Sing dlr      1.7245       1.7278         +0.19\par  Taiwan dlr    33.768       33.810         +0.12\par  Korean won   1150.00      1151.90         +0.17\par  Baht           39.60        39.83         +0.58\par  Peso           54.98        54.78         -0.36\par  Rupiah       8380.00      8383.00         +0.04\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     110.96       118.74         +7.01\par  Sing dlr      1.7245       1.7341         +0.56\par  Taiwan dlr    33.768       34.753         +2.92\par  Korean won   1150.00      1185.80         +3.11\par  Baht           39.60        43.08         +8.79\par  Peso           54.98        53.38         -2.91\par  Rupiah       8380.00      8940.00         +6.68.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031002dza200267\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
