\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Baht at 3-yr highs, others watchful.  \b0\par\par\uc2 800 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Oktober 2003\par 06:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Oct 2 (Reuters) - Most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stayed\par in sight of their recent highs on Thursday, helped by buoyant\par stock markets, with the Thai baht  leading the way as it\par explored three-year highs.\par     Dealers said markets were still on the watch for\par dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by their respective central banks,\par amid talk that the Bank of Japan might have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  early on\par to curb the yen's  rise.\par     "The overriding question at this point in time is on the\par dollar/yen," said Sameer Goel, analyst at Bank of America in\par Singapore.\par     "If you do believe that dollar/yen is actually floored at\par 110 yen and its going to be defended vigorously by the MOF\par (Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ), then obviously there is not much\par downside to dollar/Asia in general," he said.\par     The baht was pressing against 39.70 per dollar, its\par strongest since July 2000, after first hitting the level in New\par York trade. It has risen by about 8.5 percent so far this year.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Late on Thursday morning, Moody's Investor Services placed\par Thailand's foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ratings on review for possible\par upgrade, citing the strength of the economy.\par     The baht has rallied since the Bank of Thailand said on\par Wednesday that it was at an appropriate level, was not\par threatening exports, and that the bank had not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par stop its rise.\par     Commerce Minister Adisai Bodharamik also said that even if\par the baht strengthened to 38-39 per dollar by next year, exports\par would still be competitive.\par     Goel said the baht, like most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , would\par remain supported by optimism over Asia's economic recovery and\par by foreign investment flows into the region's stock markets.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FEARS\par     But elsewhere, worries about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par keep \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weak persisted.\par     Helped by equity-related dollar sales, the South Korean won\par   rose to near 1,150 per dollar, a level it has failed\par to convincingly breach in the last week due to dollar-buying\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Korean authorities.\par     Dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said state banks had pulled the won\par down to a near one-week low on Wednesday, a move they suspected\par was on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Data on Thursday showed\par Korean reserves rose by over $5 billion in September to $141.5\par billion.\par     Finance Minister Kim Jin-pyo said it was not necessary for\par the won to match the strength of other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if\par those economies were growing faster than that of Korea.\par     The Singapore dollar        closed in on four-month highs\par past 1.7230 per dollar, but players were cautious on rumours\par that Wednesday's U.S. dollar purchases by some local and\par foreign banks were on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of\par Singapore.\par     Still, dealers said the U.S. dollar sales by corporates,\par spotted in the past couple of sessions, were likely to continue\par and that would limit the Sing dollar's downside.\par     Dealers said the U.S. dollar sales, led by a local bank and\par a state enterprise, were likely related to either the purchase\par of stakes in two Indonesian state banks or to hedging of new\par quarter requirements.\par     Indonesian is expected to complete the sales of majority\par stakes in Bank Internasional Indonesia Tbk (BNII.JK) and PT\par Bank Lippo Tbk (LPBN.JK) by next month. The sales are expected\par to raise around $500 million.\par     Dealers in Jakarta said the market was expecting foreign\par inflows related to sale of the banks to start flowing into the\par market by the middle of the month.\par     "I guess most major players have already priced in those\par inflows. But smaller local players will try to play up the\par theme," said a dealer at European bank in Singapore.\par     The rupiah        rose to touch 8,360 per dollar, its\par highest since July. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has risen close to seven\par percent so far this year. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0315\par GMT\par  Change on the day\par  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     110.87       111.24         +0.33\par  Sing dlr      1.7237       1.7278         +0.24\par  Taiwan dlr    33.780       33.810         +0.09\par  Korean won   1150.10      1151.90         +0.16\par  Baht           39.72        39.83         +0.28\par  Peso           54.87        54.78         -0.16\par  Rupiah       8367.00      8383.00         +0.19\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     110.87       118.74         +7.10\par  Sing dlr      1.7237       1.7341         +0.60\par  Taiwan dlr    33.780       34.753         +2.88\par  Korean won   1150.10      1185.80         +3.10\par  Baht           39.72        43.08         +8.46\par  Peso           54.87        53.38         -2.72\par  Rupiah       8367.00      8940.00         +6.85.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031002dza2000xf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
