\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Steady Late; Stuck In Tight Range Vs US Dlr  \b0\par\par\uc2 569 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2003\par 10:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was steady late Thursday, after moving in a very tight range amid a lack of strong interest to trade in the local market, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Around 0810 GMT, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7338, barely changed from S$1.7342 late in Asia Wednesday. The U.S. dollar traded between S$1.7320 and S$1.7340 intraday.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar slipped to its session low of S$1.7320 early in the session after comments by Federal Reserve officials overnight provided market participants with further incentive to sell the already weak U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The fall, however, turned out to be brief, as the U.S. dollar recovered to S$1.7330-S$1.7340 by midday, mirroring its rise back up above Y112 against the yen, dealers said. By late Thursday, the U.S. dollar had slipped to just below that mark, trading at Y111.95.  \par \par \uc2 Market participants in Singapore remained especially cautious over the possibility that the local dollar's strength may prompt the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit the rise, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 United Overseas Bank said in a research report that there had been "pockets of talk" that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy U.S. dollars earlier in the week, though dealers said this seemed highly unlikely.  \par \par \uc2 Even so, trade in the Singapore market has been very thin over the past two sessions, especially with the MAS' monetary policy statement due early next month.  \par \par \uc2 Market participants said they generally think the MAS is comfortable with the current Singapore dollar levels and thus don't expect any change to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's currently neutral policy stance.  \par \par \uc2 Over the next few sessions, dealers expect the U.S. dollar to stay between S$1.7300 and S$1.7400 against the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Prices of Singapore government bonds ended slightly lower Thursday after giving up their early gains on profit-taking, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Local bonds had opened higher after an overnight rise in U.S. Treasurys, but the gains were eroded as selling interest emerged by late afternoon.  \par \par \uc2 At the end of the session, the yield on two-year bonds was one basis point higher at 1.14%, while at the longer end of the curve, the yield on 10-year bonds rose three basis points to 3.56%. The yield on the longest tenor, the 15-year bonds, rose four basis points to close at 4.01%.  \par \par \uc2 Interest rate swaps moved generally in tandem with the bond yields, with the two-year offer rising four basis points to 1.40%, while the five-year rose two basis points to 2.58%. The 10-year offer was three basis points higher at 3.71%.  \par \par \uc2 The spread between two- and 10-year swaps narrowed to 231 basis points from 232 basis points late Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 In the local money market, rates were mostly steady with the overnight offer unchanged at 0.5000%.  \par \par \uc2 Prices quoted in this report are pre-settlement bids obtained from dealers and are subject to change. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg}}}\par \par \uc2 -By Izham Ahmad, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-415-4150;  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par izham.ahmad@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Kevin Lim  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020030925dz9p000eh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
