\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Keep highs in sight, wary of c.banks.  \b0\par\par\uc2 692 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2003\par 10:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Sept 23 (Reuters) - Wariness of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept a lid on Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Tuesday, but\par they held on to most of the sharp gains made after the Group of\par Seven's weekend call for more flexible exchange rates.\par     A holiday in Tokyo kept the Japanese yen        steady\par around 112 per dollar in Asia, but the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moved to\par three-year highs as London trade kicked in.\par     Analysts said Asian central banks appeared to have adjusted\par their appetite for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength to allow a broader U.S.\par dollar weakening, but they were unlikely to stay out of the\par market altogether and would continue to slow the appreciation.\par     More money is however chasing the bet of further Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains and some of that spilled over into the two-decade\par old Hong Kong dollar peg.\par     In an unusual move, the spot Hong Kong dollar        rose\par against the U.S. dollar as players unwound positions that had\par been pricing in a devaluation.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the Hong Kong dollar, pegged at 7.80 to the\par U.S. dollar, rose as high as 7.7050. In tandem, one-year Hong\par Kong dollar forwards  fell to a discount for the U.S.\par dollar for the first time since 2001.\par  \par     The Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bought U.S. dollars and\par reaffirmed its commitment to the fixed exchange rate regime.\par     "The foray was driven by the market removing the hedges it\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 had taken on Hong Kong dollar devaluation after an improvement  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in the yuan sentiment," said Bhanu Baweja, UBS strategist in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Expectations of Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength saw Chinese yuan  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 one-year non-deliverable forwards rise to a record premium of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 3,650 points to the U.S. dollar, dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  THREAT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Taiwan dollar rose to 13-month highs, before  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar purchases capped the move, dealers in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Singapore dollar pulled back from three-month  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 highs, but was still stronger than late Monday levels. The  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 market was cautious amid talk that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had called  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 up banks late on Monday to check their positions.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Thai baht stayed in sight of Monday's three-year  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 high and dealers in Bangkok said talk that the Bank of Thailand  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 might come up with more measures to curb speculative trade kept  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 players wary of taking aggressive positions.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The most vocal opposition to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains continued to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 come from South Korean authorities, although the won  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 was only a touch below its near three-year highs hit  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 on Monday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The latest salvo against the won came from Park Bong-kyu, a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 deputy minister at the commerce ministry, who said a large  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 number of Korean firms would export at a loss when the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar/won exchange rate was below 1,170 won.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Still, analysts said authorities in Asia were unlikely to\par aggressively counter the U.S. dollar's weakening.\par     "This (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) will continue but not to the extent we\par have seen before," said Marios Maratheftis, an economist at\par Standard Chartered.\par     The Indonesian rupiah        jumped to one-month highs,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 catching up with gains in other regionals after a holiday on  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Monday. The Philippine peso held to the weaker side of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 55 per dollar. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0817 GMT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     111.03       112.35         +1.19\par  Sing dlr      1.7295       1.7323         +0.16\par  Taiwan dlr    33.735       33.805         +0.21\par  Korean won   1150.10      1151.20         +0.10\par  Baht           39.95        39.99         +0.10\par  Peso           54.93        55.07         +0.25\par  Rupiah       8415.00      8465.00         +0.59\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     111.03       118.74         +6.94\par  Sing dlr      1.7295       1.7341