\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Mixed on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears before G7.  \b0\par\par\uc2 681 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2003\par 05:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Sept 18 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were wary\par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday as traders wrestled with\par uncertainty over the fate of the yen  ahead of a weekend\par Group of Seven meeting likely to debate Asia's manipulation of\par exchange rates.\par     Dealers said with the yen perched on the crucial 116 per\par U.S. dollar level, beyond which the Bank of Japan is expected\par to step to weaken it, players in other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were\par reluctant to take aggressive positions.\par     Talk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pushed the South Korean won\par   a touch lower early. The Taiwan dollar\par lingered around its Wednesday close, and dealers in Singapore\par said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was in the market early on.\par  \par     "All are watching 116 (yen)," said Philip Wee, strategist\par at DBS Bank in Singapore.\par     "Doubts are still there, despite the G7, on whether the BOJ\par will give way," he added.\par     Speculation that Asian central banks would ease their grip\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 over their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has grown ahead of the G7 and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 International Monetary Fund meetings, where the policies of  \par \par \uc2 China and Japan, in particular, and Asia, in general, are  \par \par \uc2 expected to be criticised.  \par \par \uc2 Balance of payment surpluses and rallying stock markets  \par \par \uc2 have raised appreciation pressure on Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . To  \par \par \uc2 protect export competitiveness, central banks have been  \par \par \uc2 absorbing a large part of those inflows, reflected in the rise  \par \par \uc2 in the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to over $1.66  \par \par \uc2 trillion.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. and European policymakers argue that Asian  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cost their manufacturing sectors both jobs and  \par \par \uc2 markets, and has distorted the market's adjustment to a  \par \par \uc2 ballooning U.S. current account deficit.  \par \par \uc2 The Chinese yuan's perceived undevaluation came under more  \par \par \uc2 criticism from America's largest manufacturing group which  \par \par \uc2 threatened on Wednesday to file a trade complaint.  \par \par \uc2 But European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governing Council member Ernst  \par \par \uc2 Welteke urged caution in changing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  arrangements such as  \par \par \uc2 the Chinese yuan's peg to the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 LOCAL THEMES  \par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, local themes dominated. The Singapore dollar  \par \par \uc2 was weighed on by Wednesday's data showing that exports  \par \par \uc2 had posted a second successive monthly fall in August.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said slowing exports were likely to raise doubts  \par \par \uc2 over the strength of the Singapore dollar ahead of a monetary  \par \par \uc2 policy review in October.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Some players believe the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might ease policy to\par boost economic recovery by targetting a weaker exchange rate.\par     The Thai baht        was a touch weaker, and dealers in\par Singapore said some foreign funds were still trying to offload\par long baht positions.\par     The market was long of baht when last week the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 of Thailand slapped capital restrictions to discourage  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 speculative trading in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, a move which  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 stemmed some of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's momentum.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine peso fell to a three-week low, still  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 reeling from government's admission on that that it would miss  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 its deficit budget target in August.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A government source on Thursday told Reuters that the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 August budget deficit was likely to hit 17 to 18 billion pesos  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ($308 to $327 million), more than double the monthly target.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesian rupiah touched a near two-week low  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 and dealers in Jakarta said some foreign funds were spotted  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 buying U.S. dollars.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0318 GMT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     116.05       116.28         +0.20\par  Sing dlr      1.7478       1.7523         +0.26\par  Taiwan dlr    34.087       34.090         +0.01\par  Korean won   1170.10      1171.00         +0.08\par  Baht           40.59        40.57         -0.05\par  Peso           55.23        55.15         -0.14\par  Rupiah       8483.00      8465.00         -0.21\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     116.05       118.74         +2.32\par  Sing dlr      1.7478       1.7341         -0.78\par  Taiwan dlr    34.087       34.753         +1.95\par  Korean won   1170.10      1185.80         +1.34\par  Baht           40.59        43.08         +6.13\par  Peso           55.23        53.38         -3.35\par  Rupiah       8483.00      8940.00         +5.39.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030918dz9i000rt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
