\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Focus on stocks,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , China.  \b0\par\par\uc2 656 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2003\par 05:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Sept 15 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were caught\par between a number of conflicting factors on Monday, including\par weak U.S. data, falling north Asian stock markets and Europe's\par fresh criticism of the region's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policies.\par     The yen        remained steady with Japanese markets closed\par for a holiday. The euro  was under slight pressure after\par Swedish voters decided not to join the single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but the\par U.S. dollar continued to be undermined by Friday's weak retail\par and consumer confidence data.\par     The Thai baht        was among the few \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to rise,\par recovering from a sharp fall after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last week\par imposed short-term capital controls to curb speculation.\par     Chinese non-deliverable forwards (NDF) showed a rising\par premium on the yuan after Europe's top financial officials\par again urged China and Japan to share the burden of the U.S.\par current account adjustment.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  There were specific calls for China\par to shift from a virtually fixed dollar peg to managing the yuan\par against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The one-year yuan NDF premium           hit 1,900,\par equalling a record high struck in June, and pricing the yuan\par   at around 8.09 in a year, compared to the narrow\par 8.2760/8.2800 band it is managed in.\par     James Malcolm, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at JP Morgan, said the\par debate over Asia's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and policies would surely\par heat up heading into the Group of Seven meeting on the weekend,\par and it was likely regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would\par moderate.\par  \par     "I don't think there's anything new from G7 for Asia as a\par whole, but it is a continued build-up of pressure," he said.\par     "The direction is very clear, a downside dollar bias. But\par it is really a question of how it is managed in terms of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," he said.\par     ASIA WON'T BUCKLE YET\par     U.S. Fed data showed Asian central banks remained heavy\par buyers of U.S. treasuries and agency debt in early September.\par     Bhanu Baweja, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at UBS, said that judging\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 by the indifference of the yen to recent euro and dollar moves  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 and the recent measures by the Bank of Thailand, Asia had not  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 succumbed to the growing pressure to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  less.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We feel that for Asia to be seen giving in to global  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 demands of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  flexibility that are once again likely to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 be made at the G7 and IMF meetings in Dubai later this month,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 it is important that the hopes on global reflation continue  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 push foreign money into Asian equities," Baweja said in a note.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Korean won             weakened on Monday as\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 markets were weighed down by the damage and cost of Typhoon  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Maemi, falling stocks and the fear of dollar-buying  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Korean markets had been shut for three days of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 holidays.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The Taiwan dollar          fell on fears foreign investment\par into its stock markets was waning.\par     The Singapore dollar        stayed near Friday's lows, with\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 market worried that recent U.S. dollar buying by local banks  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 was on behalf of the authorities.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0310 GMT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.31       117.01         -0.26\par  Sing dlr      1.7513       1.7514         +0.01\par  Taiwan dlr    34.145       34.100         -0.13\par  Korean won   1173.40      1170.00         -0.29\par  Baht           40.61        40.80         +0.47\par  Peso           55.00        54.99         -0.02\par  Rupiah       8448.00      8445.00         -0.04\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.31       118.74         +1.22\par  Sing dlr      1.7513       1.7341         -0.98\par  Taiwan dlr    34.145       34.753         +1.78\par  Korean won   1173.40      1185.80         +1.06\par  Baht           40.61        43.08         +6.08\par  Peso           55.00        53.38         -2.95\par  Rupiah       8448.00      8940.00         +5.82.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030915dz9f0010g\par }\page {\pa