\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Sing dlr slips as SARS confirmed.  \b0\par\par\uc2 654 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 2003\par 11:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Sept 9 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar slipped\par late on Tuesday after the government confirmed the world's\par first case of the deadly SARS virus since the World Health\par Organisation declared a global outbreak over in July.\par     The Singapore dollar        slipped past $1.7570 per U.S.\par dollar in late trade after the Ministry of Health said a\par 27-year old man had tested positive for the Severe Acute\par Respiratory Syndrome virus, but it remained clear of Monday's\par lows.\par     Before the confirmation, the Singapore dollar had rebounded\par about three-quarters of a cent after falling to a one-month low\par of 1.7618 in New York trade on initial reports of the SARS\par case.\par     "The impact on price action was very much muted. I don't\par see much speculative flows as such," said a dealer at a foreign\par bank in Singapore.\par     Analysts said if it was an isolated case, which the\par government said it was, any impact on the Singapore dollar\par would be brief.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  SARS killed over 800 people in a global\par outbreak, including 33 in Singapore, and savaged Asian\par economies earlier this year.\par     BAHT RALLIES\par     Elsewhere, the Thai baht        hit a 14-month high, and\par dealers in Bangkok suspected the Bank of Thailand had\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through local banks to cap the rise when it hit\par 40.43 per U.S. dollar, its strongest since July 2002.\par     Dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was not as aggressive as\par previous bouts, and that had left the market looking for more\par gains.\par     David Simmonds, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Royal Bank of\par Scotland in Singapore, said Thailand's economic outperformance\par should allow authorities to be comfortable with some \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strength.\par     "It would be unrealistic to expect Thailand to stand\par completely out of the way of appreciation, one has to be a\par little bit wary. But by and large, I do think we are seeing a\par catch up to fundamentals here," he added.\par     A senior dealer at a local bank in Thailand said players\par were targetting 40.25 as the next level to test. However, he\par said he had heard some state enterprises were looking to buy\par dollars around those levels.\par    The South Korean won                   rose to a two-week\par high of 1,168.0 per dollar, helped by equity inflows. The Bank\par of Korea policy meeting left interest rates steady, and the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor voiced concern that an anticipated\par recovery was yet to appear.\par     Dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cited \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par as the won rose through 1,170. Seoul's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market is\par closed from Wednesday to Friday for Chosuk holidays.\par     The Philippine peso        eased to a near two-week low of\par 55.20 per dollar as dealers said the market focused on hearings\par in the Senate looking into the business dealings of President\par Gloria Macapagal Arroyo's husband.\par     The Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it was not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par prop up the peso, which it said was falling amid a lack of\par dollar inflows due to "non-economic factors". \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS\par U.S. DOLLAR AT 0911 GMT\par  Change on the day\par  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     116.30       117.04         +0.64\par  Sing dlr      1.7571       1.7564         -0.04\par  Taiwan dlr    34.097       34.129         +0.09\par  Korean won   1170.00      1171.50         +0.13\par  Baht           40.45        40.75         +0.74\par  Peso           55.20        55.13         -0.12\par  Rupiah       8458.00      8480.00         +0.26\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     116.30       118.74         +2.10\par  Sing dlr      1.7571       1.7341         -1.31\par  Taiwan dlr    34.078       34.753         +1.98\par  Korean won   1170.00      1185.80         +1.35\par  Baht           40.45        43.08         +6.50\par  Peso           55.15        53.38         -3.21\par  Rupiah       8458.00      8940.00         +5.70.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030909dz99001sa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
