\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Singapore dlr falls on SARS fears.  \b0\par\par\uc2 645 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 2003\par 05:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Sept 9 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar fell\par early on Tuesday on news of a possible return of the deadly\par SARS virus, which had killed 33 people on the island and pushed\par the economy to the verge of recession earlier in the year.\par     Other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rebounded after losses on on Monday,\par as the Japanese yen  rose from its lows against the U.S.\par dollar and as equity markets looked poised for gains.\par  \par     The Thai baht        strengthened to 14-month highs, and\par the Taiwan dollar closed in on a year high hit last week.\par     The Korean won                   rose to just shy of\par Friday's high, and the Bank of Korea left interest rates steady\par at its September meeting.\par     The Singapore dollar        fell to a one-month low of\par 1.7618 in New York trade before recovering about half a cent in\par early trade, dealers said.\par     Late on Monday, Singapore's Ministry of Health said initial\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2  tests showed one man had tested positive for the Severe Acute   \par \par \uc2  Respiratory Syndrome virus. It was believed to be an isolated   \par \par \uc2  case, and a news conference would be held on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2  The World Health Organisation said the case was not yet   \par \par \uc2  being viewed as a return of the deadly virus, which killed more   \par \par \uc2  than 800 people and savaged many Asian economies earlier this   \par \par \uc2  year.   \par \par \uc2  "At this stage, we are treating it as a suspected case - a   \par \par \uc2  perplexing case - but we're not treating it as probable SARS,"   \par \par \uc2  said Peter Cordingley, WHO's head of public information in the   \par \par \uc2  Western Pacific region.   \par \par \uc2  Dealers said rumours of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary   \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  in New York trade helped the Sing dollar   \par \par \uc2  recover some ground, and wariness of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was   \par \par \uc2  likely to keep Sing dollar in a 1.7580-1.7630 range.   \par \par \uc2  IMPACT LIKELY BRIEF   \par \par \uc2  Analysts said if it was an isolated case, any impact on the   \par \par \uc2  Singapore dollar would be brief.   \par \par \uc2  "I don't think people are taking huge short (Sing dollar)   \par \par \uc2  positions and I don't believe this would have any impact on the   \par \par \uc2  October monetary policy review," said Bhanu Baweja, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  strategist at UBS Warburg.   \par \par \uc2  Dealers said foreign funds and investment banks were taking   \par \par \uc2  positions ahead of the policy review, with some speculating   \par \par \uc2  that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which uses exchange rate rather than   \par \par \uc2  interest rate as its main policy tool, might allow more   \par \par \uc2  stimulus.   \par \par \uc2  In July, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased policy by lowering the   \par \par \uc2  centre of its exchange rate band. Most analysts were surprised   \par \par \uc2  by that move as the island had received a clean bill from the   \par \par \uc2  WHO after the SARS outbreak and the economy was expected to   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Baweja said the latest SARS case could feed speculation of\par further easing and weigh down the Singapore dollar.\par     The Philippine peso        eased to a near two-week low of\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 55.20 per dollar as dealers said the market focused on hearings\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the Senate looking into the business dealings of President\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Gloria Macapagal Arroyo's husband. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0225 GMT\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     116.63       117.04         +0.35\par  Sing dlr      1.7570       1.7564         -0.03\par  Taiwan dlr    34.093       34.129         +0.11\par  Korean won   1170.10      1171.50         +0.12\par  Baht           40.62        40.75         +0.32\par  Peso           55.16        55.13         -0.05\par  Rupiah       8470.00      8480.00         +0.12\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     116.63       118.74         +1.81\par  Sing dlr      1.7570       1.7341         -1.30\par  Taiwan dlr    34.093       34.753         +1.94\par  Korean won   1170.10      1185.80         +1.34\par  Baht           40.62        43.08         +6.06\par  Peso           55.16        53.38         -3.22\par  Rupiah       8470.00      8940.00         +5.55.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030909dz99000e4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
