\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Mostly easier, Bush comments in focus.  \b0\par\par\uc2 681 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 2003\par 11:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Sept 5 (Reuters) - Most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  eased\par on Friday as U.S. President George W. Bush joined the debate on\par China's yuan, the fixed value of which is a major factor\par limiting regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation.\par  \par     Bush told CNBC China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policies were unfair and\par that Washington would "deal with it accordingly".\par     "We expect our trading partners to treat our people fairly\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2  - our producers and workers and farmers and manufacturers -   \par \par \uc2  and we don't think we're being treated fairly when a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Bush said Treasury Secretary John Snow had delivered that\par message strongly when he was in Beijing this week.\par     The comments came a day after Japan heavily \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par pull the yen        down from a 3-=   month peak against the\par U.S. dollar and as China continued to insist it would move only\par gradually towards a floating \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Canadian Finance Minister John Manley told Reuters Snow\par would be keen to discuss Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy at this\par month's meeting of leading industrialised nations in Dubai.\par     The Asia Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) forum in its\par final communique said exchange rate policies should "facilitate\par orderly and balanced external adjustment."\par     Analysts said while Bush's comments on the issue meant the\par political stakes had been raised significantly, the debate on\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy remained inconclusive.\par     "Little by way of consensus was reached on China's exchange\par rate policy," said UBS strategist Bhanu Baweja.\par     "Snow only managed to get a Chinese commitment for an\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par eventual move to flexible exchange rate policy, something that\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Chinese authorities had already promised long before Snow's\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par arrival," he added.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said the most one could expect was a modest widening of\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the band, in which China allows the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to move, in the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par first half of 2004.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts say authorities across Asia would also continue to\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par resist significant \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation unless they gained\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par more confidence over economic recovery at home and abroad.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reflecting those views, the U.S. dollar discount priced in\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the one-year yuan non-deliverable forwards  pulled\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par back to 1,700 points, from Thursday's close of 1,875, just shy\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of its record level of 1,900 points on June 17.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar premium on one-year Hong Kong Dollar\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par forwards  moved to 47 points from an early high of 70,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par not far from Thursday's one-year low of 35 points.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Elsewhere, the South Korean won             and\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwan dollar  were the only \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to rise a notch\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par higher.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Both were helped by equity-related inflows but were\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par constrained by fear of dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by their\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par respective central banks a day after they \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par aggressively, mimicking the Bank of Japan.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar  recovered from its early\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par retreat through 1.7600 per U.S. dollar, but was still down\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against Thursday's 1.7558.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht  declined to 40.89 per dollar, before\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recovering some ground but was still off against Thursday's\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 40.73, its strongest since July 2002.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The move followed Thursday's comments by Prime Minister\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thaksin Shinawatra that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would try to keep\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength from hurting exports. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par DOLLAR AT 0834 GMT\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     116.82       116.87         +0.04\par  Sing dlr      1.7570       1.7558         -0.07\par  Taiwan dlr    34.117       34.