\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Mostly down, eye Bush talk on yuan.  \b0\par\par\uc2 717 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 2003\par 05:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Sept 5 (Reuters) - Most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stayed\par off recent highs on Friday as U.S. President George W. Bush\par joined the debate on China's yuan, the fixed value of which is\par a major factor limiting regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation.\par  \par     Bush told CNBC China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policies were unfair and\par that Washington would "deal with it accordingly".\par     "We expect our trading partners to treat our people fairly\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - our producers and workers and farmers and manufacturers -  \f28 \par \par \uc2 and we don't think we're being treated fairly when a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 is controlled by the government," Bush told CNBC.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Bush said Treasury Secretary John Snow delivered that\par message strongly when he was in Beijing this week.\par     The comments came a day after Japan heavily \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par pull the yen        down from 3-=   month peak against the U.S.\par dollar and as China continued to insist that it would move only\par gradually towards a floating \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Analysts said the comments signal that the U.S. would\par maintain pressure on China to revalue its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which has\par been pegged at around 8.3 yuan per U.S. dollar for nine years.\par     "The involvement of President Bush in the Chinese yuan\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 valuation issue significantly increases the political stakes  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 and will have a meaningful impact," said Peter Redward,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 strategist at Deutsche Bank in Singapore.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 However, Redward said China was unlikely to heed the call  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 any time soon, and at best a modest widening of the band in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 which China allows the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to move could be expected in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the next six to 12 months.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts say authorities across Asia would continue to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 resist significant \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation unless they gained  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 more confidence over economic recovery at home and abroad.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reflecting those views, the U.S. dollar discount priced in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the one-year yuan non-deliverable forwards pulled  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 back to 1,750 points, from Thursday's close of 1,875, just shy  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 of its record level of 1,900 points on June 17.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. dollar premium on one-year Hong Kong Dollar  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 forwards moved to 46 points, from an early high of 70  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 but was still far from Thursday's one-year low of 35 points.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FEARS WEIGH  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Elsewhere, the only \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to edge slightly up were the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par South Korean won             and Taiwan dollar         .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Both were helped by equity-related inflows but were  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 constrained by fear of dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by their  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 respective central banks a day after they \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 aggressively to cap \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar retreated through 1.7600 per  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. dollar, from late Thursday's 1.7558 with some major funds  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 spotted covering short U.S. dollar positions.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Thai baht edged back from 13-month highs, after  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 some local banks were spotted buying dollars late on Thursday  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 following Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra's comments that the  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would try to keep \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength from hurting  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 exports.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The baht declined to 40.89 per dollar, from Thursday's\par 40.73, its strongest since July 2002.\par     Dealers in Singapore said local corporates were hedging\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 their future dollar requirements, while three days of net  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 selling of local stocks by foreign investors has also hit  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 sentiment.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreign investors' net selling of local stocks has reached  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 more than a billion baht so far this week, and dealers say that  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 money could chase the dollar higher.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0245 GMT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     116.83       116.87  