\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Pulls back after yen  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 615 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 2003\par 11:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Sept 4 (Reuters) - Most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were\par stronger on Thursday but pulled back from early highs after\par Japan heavily \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cap the yen's  rise against\par the U.S. dollar.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  came even as the chatter among\par policymakers about Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ' undervaluation grew louder\par as the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) meeting got\par underway.\par  \par     U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow said he would keep\par pushing Asia to adopt more flexible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policies.\par     South Korean Deputy Finance Minister Kwon Tae-Shin played\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 down the impact of a rising won on his country's economy,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 saying 40 percent of its exports competed on quality and brand  \par \par \uc2 name, rather than price.  \par \par \uc2 But earlier in the day, dealers in Seoul said they had  \par \par \uc2 spotted dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Korea that   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pulled the won             to weaker levels.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thai Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra, whose recent  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 remarks had encouraged the baht hit its strongest since July  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2002, said the baht was on an uptrend, but the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 would try to prevent it from hurting exports.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts said it was unrealistic to expect Asian  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 authorities to let their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciate unless they  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 became more confident over the durability of economic recovery  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 at home and abroad.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "To the extent that the discussion is now on that is  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 something of a change, but whether that leads to a change in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 attitude of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policies I sort of doubt it," said David  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Simmonds, strategist at Royal Bank of Scotland in Singapore.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. complained that the yuan, also called the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 renminbi, was too cheap at its current pegged level of around  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 8.3 per dollar, and it was becoming a key issue ahead of the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2004 U.S. Presidential election.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     China maintains that the yuan would eventually float\par freely, but has resisted calls to speed up the process.\par     The Thai baht        pared its early gains from a 13-month\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 high of 40.73 per dollar after local banks were seen buying  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollars in large amounts, sparking rumours they were acting on  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Taiwan dollar rose to T$34.03 per U.S. dollar, its  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 strongest in more than a year, but closed local trade down at  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 34.12.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The won touched a high of 1,170.8 per dollar, before the\par dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pulled it down to 1,176.5.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar        rose to S$1.7520 per U.S.\par dollar, before it retreated to S$1.7555.\par     Sentiment remained weak as a key manufacturing activity\par report showed the Singapore economy was struggling to recover.\par     The purchasing managers' index in August eased to 51.3,\par from July's 51.4, showing the manufacturing sector was barely\par growing.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0913 GMT\par  Change on the day\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     116.87       116.15         -0.62\par  Sing dlr      1.7558       1.7566         +0.05\par  Taiwan dlr    34.120       34.095         -0.07\par  Korean won   1173.10      1174.20         +0.09\par  Baht           40.76        40.90         +0.34\par  Peso           54.95        54.76         -0.35\par  Rupiah       8480.00      8477.00         -0.04\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     116.87       118.74         +1.60\par  Sing dlr      1.7558       1.7341         -1.24\par  Taiwan dlr    34.120       34.753         +1.86\par  Korean won   1173.10      1185.80         +1.08\par  Baht           40.76        43.08         +5.69\par  Peso           54.95        53.38         -2.86\par  Rupiah       8480.00      8940.00         +5.42\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For the new Reuters scrolling global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  service please  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 click .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030904dz940035z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
