\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Thai baht buoyed, others track yen.  \b0\par\par\uc2 614 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 2003\par 05:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Sept 4 (Reuters) - The Thai baht gained nearly\par half a percent early on Thursday to its strongest in over a\par year, as Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  benefited from the Japanese yen's\par rise to three-month highs against the U.S. dollar.\par     Later, heavy \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of Japan pushed up\par the U.S. dollar, and the move also pulled most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par back from their early peaks.\par     In Thailand dealers said importers and local corporates\par were spotted buying U.S. dollars early on and there were fears\par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by authorities but foreign funds and banks were\par still lapping up the baht.\par     The baht was bought up to 40.73 per U.S. dollar, its\par strongest since July 2002, by mostly Hong Kong and Singapore\par names, a dealer at a foreign bank in Singapore said.\par     The dealer said breach of the 40.80 level, beyond which\par most players thought the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would cap gains\par aggressively, supported the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rise.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Baht stands as the lead gainer among Asian regionals,\par rising close to six percent so far this year on the back of\par strong economic growth and portfolio investments.\par     Comments by government officials over the baht's potential\par strength and Wednesday's credit ratings upgrade by Fitch\par Ratings have further buoyed market sentiment.\par     "The dollar/baht can be around 39.75 in the next three\par months," said Simon Flint, Bank of America's strategist in\par Singapore.\par     He said the baht would appreciate even more on a\par trade-weighted basis, even if gains against the U.S. dollar\par were cut short.\par     C.BANK PULLS BACK WON\par     The Taiwan dollar rose to T$34.03 per U.S. dollar, its\par strongest in more than a year, aided by U.S. dollar sales by\par exporters.\par     Equity-related inflows and exporters' dollar sales also\par pushed the South Korean won higher, before dealers spotted\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pushing the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weaker\par against Wednesday's close of local trade.\par  \par     The won touched a high of 1,170.8 per dollar, before the\par dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pulled it down to 1,176.5.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar rose to S$1.7520 per U.S. dollar,\par before it retreated to S$1.7537.\par     Sentiment remained weak as a key manufacturing activity\par report showed the economy was struggling to recover.\par     The purchasing managers' index in August eased to 51.3\par percent, from July's 51.4 percent, showing the manufacturing\par sector was barely growing.\par     "The Singapore dollar never deserved to appreciate when\par people were buying into the Asian reflation trades," Flint\par said.\par     "The economy still faces quite significant cyclical and\par structural challenges," he added.\par     Flint said the Singapore dollar could fall to 1.7900 per\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. dollar in the next three to four months. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. DOLLAR AT 0238 GMT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     116.72       116.15         -0.49\par  Sing dlr      1.7533       1.7566         +0.19\par  Taiwan dlr    34.063       34.095         +0.09\par  Korean won   1174.70      1174.20         -0.04\par  Baht           40.78        40.90         +0.29\par  Peso           54.77        54.76         -0.03\par  Rupiah       8480.00      8477.00         -0.04\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     116.72       118.74         +1.73\par  Sing dlr      1.7533       1.7341         -1.10\par  Taiwan dlr    34.063       34.753         +2.03\par  Korean won   1174.70      1185.80         +0.94\par  Baht           40.78        43.08         +5.64\par  Peso           54.77        53.38         -2.54\par  Rupiah       8480.00      8940.00         +5.42.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030904dz94000ul\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
