\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Snow,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  talk dominate.  \b0\par\par\uc2 688 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 2003\par 05:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Sept 2 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading was\par dominated for a second day by the higher yen and expectations\par that dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by regional central banks will\par be subdued while U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow is in the\par region.\par     Snow was in Tokyo on Monday and due in Beijing on Tuesday.\par     The yen        kept to steady ranges after Japanese\par authorities said a further rise in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was not\par warranted, but Asian traders braced for more aggressive\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  next week, after Snow leaves Asia.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar        stayed within a narrow band,\par the Taiwan dollar  struggled to rise past Monday's\par one-year highs and the Korean won             was a shade\par lower.\par     Even the Thai baht        was forced off 13-month highs.\par     "Dollar yen remains the driving influence in Asia," said\par Michael Jansen, markets strategist with National Australia\par Bank.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     There was pressure on the yen to rise, and it remained to\par be seen if the Bank of Japan would tolerate yen strength, he\par said.\par     "BOJ \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is only a matter of time and may take\par place only once Treasury Secretary Snow has left the region\par over the weekend," Jansen said.\par     "We could be looking towards yen strength to persist for\par most of this week and then a stronger dollar-yen exchange rate\par next week."\par     It was no surprise that the Singapore dollar had found\par heavy resistance at 1.75, traders said. The Sing dollar failed\par to capitalise on the yen's weekend rally but would be pushed\par lower if the yen pared gains, they said.\par     BAHT GIVES UP GAINS\par     The baht came under sudden downward pressure on Tuesday\par morning, after it struggled to get past a 13-month high of\par 40.91.\par  \par     One Bangkok-based trader said its drop below 41 triggered\par dollar demand both locally and from overseas players.\par     The baht has been rallying for months and with increased\par momentum in the past three weeks.\par     "A lot of the strength in the baht is coming to a close.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There have been very strong capital inflows and a lot of that  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 is skewed or possibly positioned towards how Thailand is going  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to trade as an economy in the next 12 months," Jansen said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "But that is running its course and we need to see overall  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 a much stronger period of global economic indicators for the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 baht to maintain its upside."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Markets have been confused after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last week  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was strong and that it had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , while  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 government officials forecast even higher levels for the baht.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Jansen said even if the baht continued to rise, its gains\par would be capped at 40 per dollar.\par     Elsewhere, the won continued to underperform the yen\par   on expectations the Bank of Korea would \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Philippine peso tested 55 again and then kept to the\par higher side of that figure.\par     The Indonesian rupiah        weakened slightly while\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 markets in Jakarta awaited the verdict in the treason trial of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Muslim cleric Abu Bakar Bashir, who authorities say is the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 spiritual leader of the Jemaah Islamiah network blamed for  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 violence in Southeast Asia.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But there was positive news from Indonesia's Bank  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Restructuring Agency, which announced foreign investors were  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 keen on stakes in two more banks.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0325 GMT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     116.71       116.64         -0.06\par  Sing dlr      1.7527       1.7545         +0.10\par  Taiwan dlr    34.111       34.112         +0.00\par  Korean won   1177.10      1175.30         -0.15\par  Baht           41.03        40.94         -0.22\par  Peso           54.86        54.96         +0.18\par  Rupiah       8488.00      8460.00         -0.33\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     116.71       118.74         +1.74\par  Sing dlr      1.7527       1.7341         -1.06\par  Taiwan dlr    34.111       34.753         +1.88\par  Korean won   1177.10      1185.80         +0.74\par  Baht           41.03        43.08         +5.00\par  Peso           54.86        53.38         -2.70\par  Rupiah       8488.00      8940.00         +5.33.\par   \f28 \par \par