\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Under central banks' grip, rupiah vulnerable. \b0\par\par\uc2 669 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 August 2003\par 05:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 29 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disregarded\par a rising Japanese yen and traded steady to lower on Friday\par morning, fearing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by regional central banks.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar        fell as it moved towards the\par centre of the trade-weighted band authorities manage the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in.\par     The Indonesian rupiah        continued to be pressured by\par month-end imports and market expectations that falling interest\par rates will erode its attractiveness to investors. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut overnight rates on Friday, the seventh time since May.\par     "Theoretically, the impact on the rupiah ought to be\par negative but it has been muted so far," said Vincent Low,\par markets strategist with Merrill Lynch.\par     But Low disagreed with some economists who suggest\par Indonesia ought to be less aggressive in cutting rates and\par should focus on attracting investment and building \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves as it prepares to exit an IMF funding\par programme.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "I'm not sure about using the exchange rate as a stimulus\par in a closed economy like Indonesia," Low said.\par     "Interest rates are a more direct way for macro economic\par objectives, and the way to build reserves is not through\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  but by looking for alternative sources to the\par IMF."     The Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was comfortable with some\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weakness in the rupiah, which has been one of Asia's best\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par performers this year, and other than politics, Indonesia's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economic fundamentals were sound, he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Elsewhere, a slight monetary tightening by the Philippine\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , on the heels of a government warning against\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  speculation, helped the peso  retrace losses.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  announced on Thursday after the market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par closed it is scrapping a tiered system on overnight borrowing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that paid a decreasing rate of interest and discouraged banks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from making larger deposits with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WORRIES\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht  followed what has now become a routine\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pattern, rising overnight to near 41 and paring gains in Asian\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trading. Traders said markets were worried about Bank of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thailand \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Thursday, the BOT hinted it had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to ease the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par heavy upward pressure on the baht from surging foreign\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The Taiwan dollar          rose, as stock markets rebounded\par and the yen approached 117 per dollar.\par     But the Korean won                   ceded further ground\par to the yen and the cross            moved up to 1-=   month\par highs.\par     Singapore's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was weak a day after the authorities\par announced cuts to employer contributions to the country's\par pension system.\par     "North Asia (plus Thailand and Singapore), is the best\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par place to trade global recovery, with high leverage to the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cycle, a favourable base effect from SARS-depressed first half\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par growth, and the most attractive equity valuations," JP Morgan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said in a note.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The flow pressure on local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continues to point\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to appreciation against the U.S. dollar, and central banks in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thailand and Taiwan appear to be softening their\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventionist\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stance."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The Bank of Korea remains highly supportive of the 1,170\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level, but risks remain skewed to the downside, and only in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore does the local unit appear too expensive relative to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's target zone," the note said\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0315 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.06       117.46         +0.34\par  Sing dlr      1.7574       1.7539         -0.20\par  Taiwan dlr    34.178       34.210         +0.09\par  Korean won   1178.70      1178.00         -0.06\par  Baht           41.17        41.20         +0.07\par  Peso           54.95        54.93         -0.04\par  Rupiah       8540.00      8505.00         -0.41\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.06       118.74         +1.44\par  Sing dlr      1.7574       1.7341         -1.33\par  Taiwan dlr    34.178       34.753         +1.68\par  Korean won   1178.70      1185.80         +0.60\par  Baht           41.17        43.08         +4.64\par  Peso           54.95        53.38         -2.86\par  Rupiah       8540.00      8940.00         +4.68.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030829dz8t006sn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
