\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Diverge, Sing dlr hits 2-week low. \b0\par\par\uc2 652 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 2003\par 04:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 27 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar fell to\par a two-week low early on Wednesday while the South Korean won\par and Taiwan dollar stepped further back from their recent highs.\par     The Thai baht        stayed buoyed on hopes of improving\par economic growth prospects, while consolidation of positions\par helped the Philippine peso  and Indonesian rupiah\par bounce off their recent lows.\par     The Singapore dollar        was at 1.7555 per U.S. dollar,\par its weakest since August 13 and against last Thursday's\par two-month high of 1.7328.\par     Dealers said the Singapore dollar's retreat had gathered\par pace on worries ahead of a relief package and a planned cut in\par employers' contributions to the state-run pension scheme,\par likely to be announced on Thursday.\par     Chia Woon Khien, strategist at Singapore's DBS Bank, said\par the Singapore dollar's decline was triggered after it briefly\par breached the stronger end of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's policy band\par last week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore targets the Singapore\par dollar against an undeclared basket of trade-weighted\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , of which the U.S. dollar, Japanese yen  and\par euro  are supposed to be major components.\par     "While the rest of Asia regionals can target the U.S.\par dollar on a bilateral basis, positions in Sing dollar have to\par be managed against the basket \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," she said.\par     The Singapore dollar was still on the stronger side of the\par band which suggested more downside was possible in line with\par the recent decline of the euro  and the yen's retreat\par from a one-month high against the dollar, she said.\par     Woon Khien said a test of 1.7600 per dollar was possible\par this week, depending on how the market reacts to the pension\par cuts aimed at lowering the cost of doing business in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     C.BANK WARINESS\par     Wariness over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , aimed at\par protecting export competitiveness, was seen pulling the Korean\par won             and the Taiwan dollar          off their\par recent 13-month and 11-month highs respectively.\par     Dealers in Singapore said while foreign investors had been\par buying stocks in Korea and Taiwan, the amount of net purchases\par had declined in recent sessions, raising caution on positions\par built in anticipation of capital inflows.\par     However, net selling of local stocks by foreign investors\par had little impact on the baht , which stayed in sight of\par its 13-month high hit on Monday.\par     Dealers in Singapore said players were reluctant to push\par the baht aggressively through the 41.30 per dollar level,\par fearing the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might step in to curb \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strength.\par     Thailand's finance ministry on Tuesday raised its 2003\par economic growth projection to 6.1 percent from 5.1 percent on\par robust domestic consumption and exports, lending support to\par views the baht will continue to gain on upbeat growth\par prospects.\par     The Thai economy, one of Asia's fastest-growing, surged 6.7\par percent in the first quarter, aided by a 21.3 percent jump in\par export growth. Exports rose 16.8 percent in the second quarter.\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0226 GMT\par  Change on the day\par  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.43       117.70         +0.23\par  Sing dlr      1.7550       1.7502         -0.27\par  Taiwan dlr    34.207       34.194         -0.04\par  Korean won   1170.60      1170.00         -0.05\par  Baht           41.31        41.38         +0.17\par  Peso           55.41        55.45         +0.07\par  Rupiah       8450.00      8470.00         +0.24\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.43       118.74         +1.12\par  Sing dlr      1.7550       1.7341         -1.19\par  Taiwan dlr    34.207       34.753         +1.60\par  Korean won   1170.60      1185.80         +1.30\par  Baht           41.31        43.08         +4.28\par  Peso           55.41        53.38         -3.66\par  Rupiah       8450.00      8940.00         +5.80.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030827dz8r005pl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
