\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Peso tests record lows, rest watch BOJ. \b0\par\par\uc2 641 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 2003\par 11:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 26 (Reuters) - The Philippine peso\par fell to a fresh 31-month trough on Tuesday, just shy of its\par record low, while other regionals retreated in anticipation of\par possible Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem the yen's recent rise.\par     The peso        slipped to 55.60 per U.S. dollar, its\par lowest since January 17, 2001, when it hit a record low of\par 55.75 in the turmoil of Joseph Estrada's forced exit from the\par presidency.\par     Speculation the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prop up the\par peso helped it bounce off the lows. But some dealers said the\par sharp dip in the peso had sparked a brief dollar sell-off by\par exporters prompting other players to cover their short peso\par positions.\par     "Some exporters had already placed orders within\par 55.50-55.60 range," said Rovic De Guzman, head of trading at\par the Union Bank of the Philippines.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso, already down by about seven percent since May,\par would suffer from a seasonal rise in imports and low\par remittances from workers abroad, he said.\par     Sentiment for Philippine assets has soured after a failed\par mutiny by renegade soldiers last month and on worries over\par potential instability ahead of presidential polls next year.\par     The fall came a day after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Deputy\par Governor Amando Tetangco said the bank was ready to inject\par liquidity into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market if needed.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WARINESS\par     Elsewhere, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar        fell to its lowest\par in a week, and the Korean won             and Taiwan\par dollar  retreated from 13-month and 11-month peaks\par respectively.\par  \par     The Thai baht        was up against late Monday levels, but\par off a 13-month high hit in overnight New York trade.\par     Dealers said regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped back on wariness\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that other central banks would follow suit if the Bank of Japan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par moved to cap the yen, which hit a one-month high against the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Around current levels, the market is likely to be much\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par more cautious on further yen upside in the immediate term,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said Bhanu Baweja, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at UBS.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, he said as inflows in the equity markets continue,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japanese and other Asian central banks would become more\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par comfortable with further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We see scope for a dollar/yen move to 115 over a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par three-month time frame," he said, adding the move should open\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the way for some Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strengthening.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, especially in Korea and Taiwan,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par closely monitor moves in the dollar/yen pair, which is supposed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to have a major weighting in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  baskets that central\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par banks in the region use to gauge their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par competitiveness.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Most Asian central banks have been have been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par curb \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains in the face of large capital inflows to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par their equity markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Indonesian rupiah  fell to a one-week low, as a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par softer regional bias fuelled recent long rupiah unwinding by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign players, dealers in Jakarta said. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par DOLLAR AT 0812 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.70       117.44         -0.22\par  Sing dlr      1.7502       1.7463         -0.22\par  Taiwan dlr    34.194       34.180         -0.04\par  Korean won   1170.00      1170.90         +0.08\par  Baht           41.38        41.39         +0.02\par  Peso           55.45        55.42         -0.05\par  Rupiah       8470.00      8435.00         -0.41\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.70       118.74         +0.88\par  Sing dlr      1.7502       1.7341         -0.92\par  Taiwan dlr    34.190       34.753         +1.65\par  Ko