\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Peso nears record low, rest fear BOJ. \b0\par\par\uc2 641 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 2003\par 05:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 26 (Reuters) - The Philippine peso\par hit a fresh 31-month trough on Tuesday, a breath away from its\par record low, as most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened amid fears of\par possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Japan to stem the yen's recent rise.\par     The peso        slipped to 55.60 per U.S. dollar, its\par lowest since January 17, 2001, when it hit a record low of\par 55.75 amid the turmoil of Joseph Estrada's forced exit from the\par presidency.\par     Dealers in Manila said the peso, which has lost nearly\par seven percent since May, was under pressure from a seasonal\par rise in imports and falling remittances from expatriate\par workers.\par     Sentiment for Philippine assets has soured after a failed\par mutiny by renegade soldiers last month and on worries over\par potential instability ahead of presidential polls next year.\par  \par     "From here onwards the next target will naturally be the\par all-time low of 55.75," said a dealer at a local bank.\par     Dealers said the peso backed up a bit, after some foreign\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  banks were spotted selling U.S. dollars. The move sparked \par \par \uc2  speculation the banks were acting on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The fall came a day after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Deputy \par \par \uc2  Governor Amando Tetangco said the bank was ready to inject \par \par \uc2  liquidity into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if needed. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  WARINESS \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar  posted a \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par five-session low, and the Korean won             and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwan dollar  retreated from 13-month and 11-month\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par peaks respectively.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The Thai baht        was up against late Monday levels, but\par off a 13-month high hit in overnight New York trade.\par     Dealers said regionals stepped back on wariness that any\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of Japan to cap the yen, which hit a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par one-month high against the dollar on Monday, could be mimicked\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by other regional central banks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bhanu Baweja, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at UBS, said the BOJ had\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so far due to a lack of evidence that the recent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen gains were driven by speculative flows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The fear is there. It's not just a question of speculative\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positioning as of now, but it's also a question of speculative\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positions that might build up," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, especially in Korean and Taiwan,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par closely monitor moves in the dollar/yen pair which is supposed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to have a major weighting in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  baskets central banks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the region use to gauge their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  competitiveness.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Most Asian central banks have been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gains in their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the face of large capital inflows\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to their equity markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Still, dealers in Singapore said the Sing dollar might\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par glean some support from manufacturing data, due at 0500 GMT,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and expected to show growth for the second consecutive month in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par July.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Indonesian rupiah  fell to a near one-week low,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with the softer regional bias seen fuelling recent long rupiah\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unwinding by foreign players, dealers in Jakarta said.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0256 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.50       117.44         -0.05\par  Sing dlr      1.7480       1.7463         -0.10\par  Taiwan dlr    34.189       34.180         -0.03\par  Korean won   1171.00      1170.90         -0.01\par  Baht           41.36        41.39         +0.07\par  Peso           55.57        55.42         -0.27\par  Rupiah       8485.00      8435.00         -0.59\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.50       118.74         +1.06\par  Sing dlr      1.7480       1.7341         -0.80\par  Taiwan dlr    34.189       34.753         +1.65\pa