\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - C.Banks cut gains, peso eye record lows. \b0\par\par\uc2 681 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 2003\par 11:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Aug 25 (Reuters) - Wariness over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dominated trade in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Monday,\par limiting the Philippine peso's fall and capping the rise of the\par South Korean won and Thai baht.\par     The Philippine peso slipped to a fresh 31-month low of\par 55.47 against the U.S. dollar, before ending local trade a\par touch higher, helped by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The peso is perilously close to its record low of 55.75,\par hit in January 2001 amid the turmoil of Joseph Estrada's forced\par exit from the presidency.\par  \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it was ready to inject liquidity into\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market if needed.\par     "We will provide liquidity as necessary. That policy has\par never changed," Deputy Governor Amando Tetangco said.\par     Dealers in Manila said the peso, which has lost about 6.5\par percent since May, had been under pressure from a seasonal rise\par in imports and falling remittances from overseas workers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Sentiment on Philippine assets has worsened after a failed\par mutiny last month and on worries over potential instability\par ahead of the presidential election next year.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  wrote to the finance department that it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was worried its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves, at around $16\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion, might drop in 2004 due to the huge gap between the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government's planned foreign borrowings and its debt\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par maturities.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Such news will add to concern about the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ability to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  given the reserves level," said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a dealer at a local bank in Manila.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par WON CAPPED\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won fell back after dealers in Seoul cited possible\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through state-run banks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A senior official at the Finance and Economy Ministry told\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuters that South Korea would continue to take steps to curb\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength not justified by fundamentals.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "The won's recent gain has been driven by speculative\par forces, rather than economic fundamentals," he said.\par     The comment came after the won hit a new 13-month high of\par 1,166.0 per dollar, shy of a 20-month high of 1,164.0 reached\par in July 2002.\par     Fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also capped the Taiwan\par dollar at a fresh 11-month high.\par     Simon Flint, strategist at Bank of America in Singapore,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said central banks in Asia would continue to manage \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strength until they become comfortable with the global growth\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par outlook.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will appreciate but you'll have to be patient\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and realise that the central banks are going to be quite\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cautious."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht edged back slightly from its 13-month high of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 41.32 hit on Friday in New York trade, after local players and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par some foreign funds booked profits on the move, fearing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par authorities might step in if the bath rose too far, too fast.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar lost its early gains, although its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par downside was limited by the yen's strength and investors\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par building long positions in anticipation of a global growth\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pick-up later this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said fears the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might be preparing to\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had pulled the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar off its two-month\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par highs of 1.7330 per U.S. dollar hit on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0830 GMT\par  Change on the day\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.44       117.83         +0.33\par  Sing dlr      1.7463       1.7451         -0.07\par  Taiwan dlr    34.180       34.217         +0.11\par  Korean won   1170.90      1169.50         -0.12\par  Baht           41.39        41.50         +0.27\par  Peso           55.42        55.27         -0.28\par  Rupiah       8435.00      8428.00         -0.08\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.44       118.74         +1.11\par  Sing dlr      1.7463       1.7341         -0.70\par  Taiwan dlr    34.180       34.753         +1.68\par  Korean won   1170.90      1185.80         +1.27\par  Baht           41.39        43.08         +4.08\par  Peso           55.42        53.38         -3.68\par  Rupiah       8435.00      8940.00         +5.99.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030825dz8p00izl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
