\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Strong but wary of cbanks, peso falls. \b0\par\par\uc2 756 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 2003\par 11:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 21 (Reuters) - An early spike in some Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was capped by actual and suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday, but dealers said forecasts of a\par global recovery and portfolio inflows pointed to further\par strength.\par  \par     The expection remained the Philippine peso, which ended\par local trade at another record closing low of 55.265 per dollar.\par     The South Korean won                   pulled back from a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  seven-month high of 1,171.9 per dollar, after selling from \par \par \uc2  local banks sparked speculation the authorities were behind the \par \par \uc2  move. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Taiwan dollar was blocked at an 11-month \par \par \uc2  peak of 34.225 per dollar on intermittent but aggressive \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar hit a two-month high of 1.7366 per \par \par \uc2  dollar. Traders decided to book profits rather than risk \par \par \uc2  testing the resolve of authorities by pushing deeper into the \par \par \uc2  strong side of an undisclosed policy band. \par \par \uc2  "The strength of the Singapore dollar has pushed it to the \par \par \uc2  upper half of its trade-weighted index, suggesting that \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks have risen," said Thio Chin Loo, senior \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at BNP Paribas. \par \par \uc2  She said the Singapore dollar could rise up to 1.7250, \par \par \uc2  which she calculated as the stronger end of the targeted policy \par \par \uc2  band. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "Gains beyond would depend on how much further the yen and\par other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can go," she said.\par     Dealers and analysts said most Asian central banks have\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par acted this year to limit their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength to protect\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par export competitiveness. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains also counter the easier\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par monetary policy stances many central banks have adopted this\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht  rose to a month high as the stronger\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par regional bias helped it overcome Wednesday's selling pressure,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par triggered after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it was allowing foreign\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par debt investment applications of $2.45 billion.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     That was about five times the limit it had announced when\par it relaxed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  controls last month.\par     The Indonesian rupiah rose to the stronger side of 8,400\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par per dollar for the first time since July 22, to be about four\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent higher than the lows hit after a Jakarta hotel was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bombed on August 5.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Aslim Tadjuddin, the deputy governor of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par told Reuters the strengthening of rupiah was a vote of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par confidence by foreign and domestic investors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PESO EYES RECORD LOWS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In Philippines, however, the euphoria of the expected\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economic recovery in the region was lost amid political worries\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ahead of the May presidential elections.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso  fell to 55.28 per dollar, its weakest since\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par January 2001 when it hit a record low of 55.75 amid the turmoil\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of Joseph Estrada's forced exit from the presidency.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The irony is that it (peso) should benefit from the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recovery given its export profile, but obviously the odd thing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par out here is the politics," said Claudio Piron, strategist at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Standard Chartered in Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso has fallen more than six percent from this year's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par high in May, pressured by political and security concerns,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par including a failed mutiny on July 27.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Manila said a combination of lean remittances\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from overseas workers and a seasonal peak in dollar demand from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par importers would keep the peso under pressure.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But they said the market was cautious amid speculation that\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had sold U.S. dollars around 55.20 on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A dealer at a local bank said some long U.S. dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unwinding was also spotted by players trying to shed their\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exposures ahead of a long weekend. Financial markets in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Philippines would be closed on Friday for a local holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0813 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.95       118.32         +0.31\par  Sing dlr      1.7401       1.7485         +0.48\par  Taiwan dlr    34.238       34.298         +0.20\par  Korean won   1173.0       1175.50         +0.21\par  Baht           41.54        41.65         +0.28\par  Peso           55.265       55.19         -0.14\par  Rupiah       8375.00      8415.00         +0.48\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.95       118.74         +0.67\par  Sing dlr      1.7401       1.7341         -0.34\par  Taiwan dlr    34.238       34.753         +1.53\par  Korean won   1173.0       1185.80         +1.09\par  Baht           41.54        43.08         +3.72\par  Peso           55.265       53.38         -3.41\par  Rupiah       8375.00      8940.00         +6.75.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030821dz8l00jm4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
