\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Up Late On Yen, Local Stks; Off 2-Mo High \b0\par\par\uc2 739 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 2003\par 10:24\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar was stronger late Thursday, but off a fresh two-month high, supported by a stronger yen and fund flows into the local stock market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0805 GMT, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7398, down from S$1.7488 late in Asia Wednesday. It traded between S$1.7365 and S$1.7420 intraday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar opened around S$1.7390 after its broad overnight retreat against the yen in New York. \par \par \uc2  It initially hovered around S$1.7380-S$1.7390 but dropped further to S$1.7360, its lowest in two months, mirroring its move against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Fund flows into a buoyant local stock market also aided the Singapore dollar to its two-month high, with the benchmark Straits Times Index up 0.9% at 1626.69 points late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  But the U.S. dollar managed to recoup some losses against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  midafternoon, also in line with the yen, amid concerns the sharp intraday U.S. dollar fall might cause the local \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the descent. \par \par \uc2  At the end of the session, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at Y118.00 off its session low of Y117.83, but still weaker compared with Y118.56 late Wednesday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Standard Chartered Bank said in a research report that with the local dollar having appreciated about 1% since July, "This means that we are fast approaching the limit of (\b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar) strength and the risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is increasing." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  guides the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar within a trading band against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the country's major trading partners. It occasionally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to iron out excess volatility and to keep the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within the undisclosed band. \par \par \uc2  Later Thursday, the U.S. dollar is expected to stay between S$1.7360 and S$1.7450, though trade is likely to be thinner as the weekend nears. \par \par \uc2  Prices of Singapore government bonds ended higher Thursday, but generally off their early peaks, as an overnight fall in U.S. Treasurys damped a relief rally in the local bond market. \par \par \uc2  Local bonds opened sharply higher as market participants welcomed the announcement that the MAS would auction S$1.5 billion in new 15-year bonds on Aug. 27, smaller than market expectations of between S$2 billion and S$2.5 billion. \par \par \uc2  The smaller size eased concerns that the market would be flooded with new issues and was expected to fuel a sharp rally through Thursday's session. \par \par \uc2  But some tenors trimmed their early gains as attention switched back toward the sharp overnight retreat in U.S. Treasurys and the implications for trends in the local bonds market. \par \par \uc2  At the end of the session, the yield on two-year bonds was down three basis points at 1.40%, while the yield on five-year bonds shed four basis points to 2.54%. \par \par \uc2  At the longer end of the curve, the yield on seven-year bonds was six basis points lower at 3.21%, while the yield on 10-year bonds fell seven basis points to 3.61%. \par \par \uc2  The yield on 15-year bonds was two basis points lower at 3.78%. \par \par \uc2  The above are pre-settlement closing bids obtained from dealers and are subject to minor changes. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg}}}\par \par \uc2  In the interest rate swaps market, offers were also lower, tracking local bond yields. The two-year offer slipped one basis point to 1.55%, while the five-year swap offer also slipped one basis point to 2.77%. The 10-year offer was four basis points lower at 3.82%. \par \par \uc2  The spread between two- and 10-year swaps narrowed to 227 basis points from late Wednesday's 230 basis points. \par \par \uc2  In the local money market, rates were steady as liquidity remained sufficient in the banking system. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Late Thursday     Late Wednesday\par                   bid     offer     bid     offer\par Overnight         0.8125% 0.8750%   0.8125% 0.8750%\par 3-Month           0.7500% 0.8750%   0.7500% 0.8750%\par 1-Year            0.9375% 1.0625%   0.9375% 1.0625%\par -By Izham Ahmad, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-415-4150;\par izham.ahmad@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -Edited by Kevin Lim\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030821dz8l000i4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
