\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Peso at 31-mth low, Taiwan dlr up. \b0\par\par\uc2 769 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 2003\par 05:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 20 (Reuters) - The persistent weakness of\par the Philippine peso  stuck out like a sore thumb on\par Wednesday as other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose on the back of a\par stronger Japanese yen.\par     The beleaguered peso fell to 55.18 per dollar, its lowest\par since January 2001 when it hit a record low of 55.75 amid the\par turmoil of Joseph Estrada's forced exit from the presidency\par during an army-backed popular revolt.\par     John McGowan, treasurer of HSBC, Philippines, said the\par uncertainty after recent events in the Philippines -- a failed\par mutiny and a court-ordered one-year suspension of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par Governor Rafael Buenaventura, which has been appealed -- were\par keeping the peso under pressure.\par     It was likely demand for dollars to hedge liabilities had\par increased from corporates who had been complacent during the\par peso's stability in the months before the July mutiny, he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso held a tight 55.10-55.13 range in early trade, but\par a large order for dollars pushed it through its March low of\par 55.16.\par      "I heard of a sizeable demand for dollars. It seems to be\par a temporary thing, although the move is in line with our long\par term view," said Rovic De Guzman, head of trading at the Union\par Bank of the Philippines.\par     YEN BOOSTS REGION\par     The yen's strength, derived from the Nikkei average's\par   rise to 13 month highs, boosted other regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Taiwan dollar          hit its highest since July 11,\par backed by continuing foreign equity inflows into a rising share\par market and the suspicion that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was not\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cap its gains.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar        was stuck in familiar ranges\par around 1.7480-1.7500 per U.S. dollar, although against the euro\par   it has risen for two weeks, to 1.9422 per euro from\par 2.01.\par     "The trade-weighted Sing dollar has been reasonably firm,"\par said David Simmonds, markets strategist with the Royal Bank of\par Scotland.\par     Singapore's stock markets have been enthused by the\par government's decision, announced on the weekend, to cut\par employer contributions to employees' pension funds.\par     But some \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traders worried that the move could be\par accompanied by a monetary loosening, which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par operates through the trade-weighted band for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Thai baht        was languid, following the yen with\par markets apathetic after the authorities said they saw the baht\par gradually appreciating this year and said the current strength\par was not hurting exports.\par     The Korean won                   recovered to be slightly\par stronger in local trade after a drop to 1,180 per dollar in\par offshore deals.\par     "It looks like a bear trap on the won. The false breakout\par stalled at 1181," a trader said of the drop, which was possibly\par because dollar bears had been forced to cut positions.\par  \par     The won however was shy of the sensitive 1,175 level amid\par suspicion the Bank of Korea had bought dollars this week.\par     Data on Tuesday showing a $1.87 billion rise in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves in the first half of August, following a $1.2\par billion rise in July, strengthened those fears.\par     But the Taiwan dollar's rise suggested the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par there to contain the gains may have lessened, Simmonds said.\par     "There are these big equity inflows into Taiwan. And the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CBC (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) periodically steps out of the way and lets\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Taiwan dollar strengthen when there are overwhelming\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflows."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "But, I don't think this is the beginning of the end of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  story," he said. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par AT 0245 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.62       119.55         +0.78\par  Sing dlr      1.7488       1.7515         +0.15\par  Taiwan dlr    34.306       34.353         +0.14\par  Korean won   1176.70      1179.10         +0.20\par  Baht           41.63        41.64         +0.04\par  Peso           55.14        55.12         -0.03\par  Rupiah       8440.00      8473.00         +0.39\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.62       118.74         +0.10\par  Sing dlr      1.7488       1.7341         -0.84\par  Taiwan dlr    34.306       34.753         +1.30\par  Korean won   1176.70      1185.80         +0.77\par 